{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5","id":1557559,"title":"A W20 Wolf in W5.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-13T14:43:50-08:00","id":1557559,"title":"A W20 Wolf in W5.","content":"Inspired by this conversation on the Bloodlines 2 thread.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555226-bloodlines-2-and-the-current-state-of-paradox?p=1557544#post1557544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering you'd need an elder vampire to have a realistic chance of bringing one down in single combat?<br /> <br /> Your deed name should be <i>&quot;Kills With One Punch.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Might of Thor doubles your Strength score, if I'm not mistaken. Which means if the Get has 5-6 Strength, they temporarily shoot up to Antedeluvian levels!</div> </div> </div> </div>As the title states this thread discuss the consequences of a W20 wolf appearing in W5 and how hard they'll derail things from the sheer power imbalance they existence causes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-14T13:01:36-08:00","id":1557615,"title":"","content":"Hey, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6156\" data-vbnamecard=\"6156\">Bluecho</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a>, and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12141\" data-vbnamecard=\"12141\">MarkK</a>, over here.<br /> <br /> Also, since it apparently wasn't clear:<br /> <br /> I understand that W20 and D&amp;D use radically different definitions of Strength. That was the point. Dropping a character from one game using their stats in that game into a different game isn't fair in one direction or the other. Unless you're going to actually translate the character's abilities in a fair fashion the comparison is meaningless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T18:43:13-08:00","id":1557664,"title":"","content":"But W20 and W5 use the same Strength scale. This can be inferred from W5 slavishly and bizarrely keeping the same progression of feats of Strength with one dot being crushing a beer can. The only difference is that the W5 chart is given entirely in kg instead of lbs, but it works out to the same weight.<br /> <br /> What changes here is that Gifts exist in prior editions that W5 doesn't have because V5 characters can't possibly be challenged on any front. Because if the reaction from the one true way crowd to Crinos is utter shock and disbelief and a desire to leash it with the threat of losing all Rage and powers for an entire night, they certainly don't want Might of Thor, Gift of the Spriggan, or Warp Frenzy looming over even the possibility that, if they're trying to make everyone play in the same setting, that a single Garou will splash the walls with an entire coterie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T20:14:51-08:00","id":1557665,"title":"","content":"Using a 1-5 rating scale doesn't mean the stats actually mean the same thing, because the dice mechanics and systems are largely (yes, I know you have a counter-example) different in function.<br /> <br /> This whole this was debated to death two decades ago when the CofD 1e came out and lots of people were going on about how much stronger WoD characters are than CofD ones, without actually <b>fairly</b> translating things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T21:50:20-08:00","id":1557666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557665#post1557665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a 1-5 rating scale doesn't mean the stats actually mean the same thing, because the dice mechanics and systems are largely (yes, I know you have a counter-example) different in function.<br /> <br /> This whole this was debated to death two decades ago when the CofD 1e came out and lots of people were going on about how much stronger WoD characters are than CofD ones, without actually <b>fairly</b> translating things.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds silly.<br /> <br /> World of Darkness was building up to a literal apocalypse scenario, and had every splat existing within the same continuity.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness is more stand alone adventurers, with each splat existing within its own self contained narrative. There's not really a reason for them to be demigods in Chronicles.<br /> <br /> No antedeluvians rising to consume their progeny for the vampires. Especially not when they can reduce their BP through torpor and start feeding on humans / animals again.<br /> <br /> No cosmic avatar of death trying to destroy the planet for Werewolves. Instead you're the acting police force of the spiritual border.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T22:53:03-08:00","id":1557667,"title":"","content":"Stats aside a classic garou has four major advantages over <br /> <br /> 1) its able maintain crinos warform as a stable state<br /> 2) its able to survive in the umbra without special criteria<br /> 3)it has access to a supplementry 'energy' source effectively increasing the gift battery<br /> 4) its not being slowly driven mad in a way hardwired into them<br /> <br /> Ignoring power scaling, these advantages put a classic garou leagues ahead of a w5 garou who are frankly not very good anyway.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-15T23:41:14-08:00","id":1557668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557666#post1557666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That sounds silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet it happened. And yet it happened again when V5 came out. And I see the same thing happening with this.<br /> <br /> And it's not just Str vs. Str. It's also things like what a Gift like Might of Thor would look like when translated into W5's design paradigm. When Requiem 1e came out, people lamented how much weaker vampire Disciplines were without, again, taking into account changes in context (I used to have a C&amp;P ready to go to demonstrate the math on a few common examples that weren't as subject to situation like social powers can be).<br /> <br /> Might of Thor fairly translated into W5's design paradigm isn't going to double your Str rating, but it would also probably be a more practical Gift as well (not requiring Rage and Gnosis expenditures, and diff 8 roll with duration in successes). People start throwing around Paw of the Newborn Cub like it's not a Rank 5 Silver Fang Gift which means it's exceptionally rare instead of more common Rank 1 and 2 Gifts. Etc.<br /> <br /> Even <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26986_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26986\" data-vbnamecard=\"26986\">Ragged Robin</a>'s list has a similar problem. The W20 advantages all presume protracted combat over multiple encounters that'll be able to incorporated physical and Umbral conflicts. None of the list matters to two packs engaging in a turf skirmish (or even a fight with higher stakes in the moment).<br /> <br /> The biggest difference between the Garou in W20 and the Garou in W5 doesn't even matter to mechanics. W20 is a Garou Nation that's still an organize military society that can coordinate globally and in the Umbra just talking sheer logistics. W5 is a future where that all fell apart and all the war infrastructure is gone. Of course an actual army beats scattered groups of the kids of soldiers that don't have enough high level coordination to facilitate a resistance movement using guerilla tactics. Even if the math supported W5 PCs being stronger in every individual comparison they'd still lose over a sustained fight because numbers are better than high stats in either edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T03:33:45-08:00","id":1557671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557668#post1557668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The biggest difference between the Garou in W20 and the Garou in W5 doesn't even matter to mechanics. W20 is a Garou Nation that's still an organize military society that can coordinate globally and in the Umbra just talking sheer logistics. W5 is a future where that all fell apart and all the war infrastructure is gone. Of course an actual army beats scattered groups of the kids of soldiers that don't have enough high level coordination to facilitate a resistance movement using guerilla tactics. Even if the math supported W5 PCs being stronger in every individual comparison they'd still lose over a sustained fight because numbers are better than high stats in either edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Get of Fenris:</b> <i>&quot;Skill Issue! When we became The Pure, we singlehandedly wiped out nearly all life on the planet!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T14:41:19-08:00","id":1557683,"title":"","content":"I get that's not meant to be serious, but I'm not sure what you're trying to get at; even as a joke. In Forsaken the followers of Fenris Wolf are a Forsaken Tribe, not a Pure Tribe, and didn't go about trying to wipe out all life on the planet. The Pure Tribe that wants to send humanity back to the Stone Age are the Predator Kings, who are more analogous to the Red Talons, and the other Pure don't share the same zeal on killing humans. Setting the world back to spiritual Pangaea will kill off the weak regardless by making nature &quot;properly&quot; hard to survive in.<br /> <br /> In W5 the &quot;Pure&quot; aren't a thing, and the Cult of Fenris are evil scumbags, but there's nothing indicating they even thought about mass death and destruction like that... and the Red Talons are still somehow a loyal Garou Tribe that actively kill humans in exceptionally horrific ways which everyone is OK with for some reason.<br /> <br /> So... whatever the point of mashing that all together has went over my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T17:07:12-08:00","id":1557691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557664#post1557664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But W20 and W5 use the same Strength scale. This can be inferred from W5 slavishly and bizarrely keeping the same progression of feats of Strength with one dot being crushing a beer can. The only difference is that the W5 chart is given entirely in kg instead of lbs, but it works out to the same weight.<br /> <br /> What changes here is that Gifts exist in prior editions that W5 doesn't have because V5 characters can't possibly be challenged on any front. Because if the reaction from the one true way crowd to Crinos is utter shock and disbelief and a desire to leash it with the threat of losing all Rage and powers for an entire night, they certainly don't want Might of Thor, Gift of the Spriggan, or Warp Frenzy looming over even the possibility that, if they're trying to make everyone play in the same setting, that a single Garou will splash the walls with an entire coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well to be fair the closest analog in this situation is World to chronicles conversion guides that onyx path released. Like VT:M to VT:R is an example and I'm pretty sure there's WT:A to WT:F equivalent.<br /> <br /> Granted the Upcoming Werewolf the Essentials also allegedly comes with W20 to W5 conversion guide though jury out on how detailed it could bet anything from a whole chapter breaking down how the stats should translate between editions or just some general guidelines sorted into neat bullet points. Probably the latter since allegedly Book 1 has 300 gifts and I doubt the writers would fit that much pages into a already packed book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T19:39:53-08:00","id":1557693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557683#post1557683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that's not meant to be serious, but I'm not sure what you're trying to get at; even as a joke. In Forsaken the followers of Fenris Wolf are a Forsaken Tribe, not a Pure Tribe, and didn't go about trying to wipe out all life on the planet. The Pure Tribe that wants to send humanity back to the Stone Age are the Predator Kings, who are more analogous to the Red Talons, and the other Pure don't share the same zeal on killing humans. Setting the world back to spiritual Pangaea will kill off the weak regardless by making nature &quot;properly&quot; hard to survive in.<br /> <br /> In W5 the &quot;Pure&quot; aren't a thing, and the Cult of Fenris are evil scumbags, but there's nothing indicating they even thought about mass death and destruction like that... and the Red Talons are still somehow a loyal Garou Tribe that actively kill humans in exceptionally horrific ways which everyone is OK with for some reason.<br /> <br /> So... whatever the point of mashing that all together has went over my head.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a reference to one of the Apocalypse scenarios, in which the Get of Fenris fall to Wyrm Corruption.<br /> <br /> The BSD's lure them into Malfeas, thinking they're about to get a new ally, only to find that the Wyrm had intended to replace them with the Get. What follows is the Get immediately slaughtering the BSD's in their entirety, and being transformed by the Wyrm into the physical personification of death itself. This transformation causes their entire bodies to turn stark white, and they rename themselves The Pure, before returning to the world and eradicating nearly all life.<br /> <br /> If you're wondering about my sources, I use Galliard Group. They're very passionate about World of Darkness, and have a bunch of deep dive lore videos on the subject. Most having to do with Werewolf, but occasionally branching into Mage, Vampire and Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-16T20:33:06-08:00","id":1557696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557691#post1557691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well to be fair the closest analog in this situation is World to chronicles conversion guides that onyx path released. Like VT:M to VT:R is an example and I'm pretty sure there's WT:A to WT:F equivalent.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is only for CofD 1e, and only for a few of the games. It's all very out of date now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557693#post1557693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a reference to one of the Apocalypse scenarios, in which the Get of Fenris fall to Wyrm Corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-17T10:59:43-08:00","id":1557709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557693#post1557693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a reference to one of the Apocalypse scenarios, in which the Get of Fenris fall to Wyrm Corruption.<br /> <br /> The BSD's lure them into Malfeas, thinking they're about to get a new ally, only to find that the Wyrm had intended to replace them with the Get. What follows is the Get immediately slaughtering the BSD's in their entirety, and being transformed by the Wyrm into the physical personification of death itself. This transformation causes their entire bodies to turn stark white, and they rename themselves The Pure, before returning to the world and eradicating nearly all life.<br /> <br /> If you're wondering about my sources, I use Galliard Group. They're very passionate about World of Darkness, and have a bunch of deep dive lore videos on the subject. Most having to do with Werewolf, but occasionally branching into Mage, Vampire and Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>BSDs: &quot;Ah, another tribe falls to corruption! Welcome to the fold!&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast-of-War: &quot;About that. You know how you preach how destruction is the way? Get destroyed.&quot;<br /> <br /> BSDs: *Surprised Pikachu Face*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"a