/div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557693#post1557693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a reference to one of the Apocalypse scenarios, in which the Get of Fenris fall to Wyrm Corruption.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, they basically get the short hand of the stic in every situation<br /> When the Shadow Lords fell in he Apocalypse scenario, Grandfather devoured their Totem and the Lords simply replaced them eaither absorbing but more likely eliminating the BSD<br /> ...same with the &quot;Silver Spirals&quot;/Fiery Crowns<br /> <br /> Who would have tought, amirite?<br /> <br /> But in my eyes it opened a funny and interesting situation where the BSD survivors potentially tried to seek out the Gaian Garou with valuable intel to be temporary allies, not even caring if they will be killed after the uneasly alliance - they wanted REVENGE!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T15:15:24-08:00","id":1557740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557720#post1557720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, they basically get the short hand of the stic in every situation<br /> When the Shadow Lords fell in he Apocalypse scenario, Grandfather devoured their Totem and the Lords simply replaced them eaither absorbing but more likely eliminating the BSD<br /> ...same with the &quot;Silver Spirals&quot;/Fiery Crowns<br /> <br /> Who would have tought, amirite?<br /> <br /> But in my eyes it opened a funny and interesting situation where the BSD survivors potentially tried to seek out the Gaian Garou with valuable intel to be temporary allies, not even caring if they will be killed after the uneasly alliance - they wanted REVENGE!<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And people think that the Impergium would be impossible to enact in this day and age.<br /> <br /> No, it wouldn't. The Garou Nation just doesn't have the spine to do it. You don't infect an entire species with PTSD at the genetic level, if you were doing a bad job of hunting them.<br /> <br /> Yeah, humanity may have advanced technology, but the Garou can invoke the spirit of Gremlin. Also, they can use their own collection of advanced tech, thanks to Glass Walkers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T15:44:09-08:00","id":1557741,"title":"","content":"I personally prefer W20 to W5, but I don\u2019t hate W5. And I think an Impergium style campaign, the Garou versus the Second Inquisition, maybe in a limited geographic area as a testing ground, would be an interesting choice for W5, if a little morally dark (unless they played a pack of Garou trying to stop the others from re-enacting the Impergium).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T15:57:09-08:00","id":1557742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557741#post1557741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally prefer W20 to W5, but I don\u2019t hate W5. And I think an Impergium style campaign, the Garou versus the Second Inquisition, maybe in a limited geographic area as a testing ground, would be an interesting choice for W5, if a little morally dark (unless they played a pack of Garou trying to stop the others from re-enacting the Impergium).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think a fight with the SI is even feasibly possible for Garou, due to the effects of Delirium.<br /> <br /> Even the strongest willed humans, who can muster up the courage to fight back, do so in a crazed / manic fashion. Essentially throwing caution to the wind and charging in blindly. Not the kind of behavior that lends itself well to a systematic or calculated hunting strategy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then with Changelings, you have The Mists, that just cause them to forget everything they experienced.<br /> <br /> Demons can just go into Apocalyptic form, and any soldier who doesn't immediately shoot themselves in the head out of mind rending horror, would become enthralled by their presence.<br /> <br /> If the Second Inquisition is an annoyance for vampires, it would be a laughing stock for the other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-18T20:29:37-08:00","id":1557750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557742#post1557742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think a fight with the SI is even feasibly possible for Garou, due to the effects of Delirium.<br /> <br /> Even the strongest willed humans, who can muster up the courage to fight back, do so in a crazed / manic fashion. Essentially throwing caution to the wind and charging in blindly. Not the kind of behavior that lends itself well to a systematic or calculated hunting strategy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then with Changelings, you have The Mists, that just cause them to forget everything they experienced.<br /> <br /> Demons can just go into Apocalyptic form, and any soldier who doesn't immediately shoot themselves in the head out of mind rending horror, would become enthralled by their presence.<br /> <br /> If the Second Inquisition is an annoyance for vampires, it would be a laughing stock for the other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably why Hunter: the Parenting has them buddying up with Pentex (any references you see to &quot;the Coalition&quot; involve this alliance of convenience). If they get with them, or perhaps DNA, they can get access to anti-werebeast countermeasures like drugs that suppress the Delirium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-19T02:57:00-08:00","id":1557755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557750#post1557750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably why Hunter: the Parenting has them buddying up with Pentex (any references you see to &quot;the Coalition&quot; involve this alliance of convenience). If they get with them, or perhaps DNA, they can get access to anti-werebeast countermeasures like drugs that suppress the Delirium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, another <b>H:tP</b> fan!<br /> <br /> But yeah, pretty much everybody except D were losing their shit when the werewolf revealed themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-27T18:25:56-08:00","id":1557955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557668#post1557668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The biggest difference between the Garou in W20 and the Garou in W5 doesn't even matter to mechanics. W20 is a Garou Nation that's still an organize military society that can coordinate globally and in the Umbra just talking sheer logistics. W5 is a future where that all fell apart and all the war infrastructure is gone. Of course an actual army beats scattered groups of the kids of soldiers that don't have enough high level coordination to facilitate a resistance movement using guerilla tactics. Even if the math supported W5 PCs being stronger in every individual comparison they'd still lose over a sustained fight because numbers are better than high stats in either edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honstly a W20 garou finding themselves in W5 is a really cursed premise for an Isakai. Like it's going eithe be really funny or really sad. Either way there will be collateral damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-31T03:07:51-08:00","id":1558040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1557955#post1557955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honstly a W20 garou finding themselves in W5 is a really cursed premise for an Isakai. Like it's going eithe be really funny or really sad. Either way there will be collateral damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>&quot;The fuck do you mean we're racist? Do you have any idea the kind of shit Irish people have been subjected to?&quot;</i> - <b>Fianna.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Uhhh, who the hell let all these men into our cairn?&quot;</i> - <b>Black Furies.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Fuck no, we're not accepting white people!&quot;</i> - <b>Uktena</b><br /> <br /> 