their Kinfolk. Many of whom are wolves. This is what centers them, because they haven't quite gotten the hang of outlasting their tool-using form like Mokole, and - listen closely, because this is important - <b>if the wolves died, the remaining Garou would cease to be Garou. The game is making a statement about extinction here.</b><br /> <br /> Really, &quot;connection to human society&quot;. What is this, Vampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T19:09:56-08:00","id":1558305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558304#post1558304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Human society</i>? No. Garou have always been apart from it, but not their Kinfolk. Many of whom are wolves. This is what centers them, because they haven't quite gotten the hang of outlasting their tool-using form like Mokole, and - listen closely, because this is important - <b>if the wolves died, the remaining Garou would cease to be Garou. The game is making a statement about extinction here.</b><br /> <br /> Really, &quot;connection to human society&quot;. What is this, Vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're connected to humanity in the sense that they are forced to take humans (or wolves) as their mates. That means they can't just whole sale slaughter the humans and be done with it.<br /> <br /> If the Garou were allowed to safely mate with other Garou and produce healthy offspring from it, they might stop viewing humanity as essential to their survival, and view them as nothing more than an existential threat which needs to be eliminated. Much like the Red Talons, who refuse to accept Homid born into their tribe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 05-11-2026, 06:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T22:21:59-08:00","id":1558309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558305#post1558305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're connected to humanity in the sense that they are forced to take humans (or wolves) as their mates. That means they can't just whole sale slaughter the humans and be done with it.<br /> <br /> If the Garou were allowed to safely mate with other Garou and produce healthy offspring from it, they might stop viewing humanity as essential to their survival, and view them as nothing more than an existential threat which needs to be eliminated. Much like the Red Talons, who refuse to accept Lupus born into their tribe.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>None of those were the words you used in the prior post. Also, you trailed off at the end there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T23:09:32-08:00","id":1558311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558309#post1558309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of those were the words you used in the prior post. Also, you trailed off at the end there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless I'm super hallucinating, I'm pretty sure you're wrong. There seems to have been a communication error on your end.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: OH, I think I see the problem. You thought my post was being issued as a reply to the Lupus.<br /> <br /> No, it was just a generic Metis dialog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 02-14-2026, 02:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T08:29:30-08:00","id":1558318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558311#post1558311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unless I'm super hallucinating, I'm pretty sure you're wrong. There seems to have been a communication error on your end.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: OH, I think I see the problem. You thought my post was being issued as a reply to the Lupus.<br /> <br /> No, it was just a generic Metis dialog.</div> </div> </div> </div>...No, it falls short of actual Crinos-born dialog, too. To a lupus Garou or otherwise, there would be no mention of human society. Human and wolf sides, perhaps, but not &quot;human society&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T12:41:54-08:00","id":1558322,"title":"","content":"Anyway moving on how much damage a legacy garou do to W5 setting. Assuming the stat conversion falls in the legacy garou favour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T14:13:49-08:00","id":1558325,"title":"","content":"Practically zero to an immeasurable ton depending on the stats, and other considerations (like metaphysical changes).<br /> <br /> A legacy Lost Cub that had their First Change five seconds before being plopped in W5 isn't better off than a base-line starting level W5 PC (though splat picks will adjust depending on the context of the kind of damage you mean). An Elder with 2,000 XP spent at legacy rates, full access to their pack benefits even if not their packmates and Sept benefits even if not their Sept, can use Gifts that summon legacy spirits, can interact with the Umbra on legacy terms, has a bunch of legacy Fetishes and Talons they carry around... well I think you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-15T14:40:35-08:00","id":1558345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558325#post1558325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practically zero to an immeasurable ton depending on the stats, and other considerations (like metaphysical changes).<br /> <br /> A legacy Lost Cub that had their First Change five seconds before being plopped in W5 isn't better off than a base-line starting level W5 PC (though splat picks will adjust depending on the context of the kind of damage you mean). An Elder with 2,000 XP spent at legacy rates, full access to their pack benefits even if not their packmates and Sept benefits even if not their Sept, can use Gifts that summon legacy spirits, can interact with the Umbra on legacy terms, has a bunch of legacy Fetishes and Talons they carry around... well I think you get the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>So how much would they really break the setting from the scale of terrestrial to Lunar Exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-15T17:26:53-08:00","id":1558347,"title":"","content":"Apples and oranges?<br /> <br /> Garou were designed to fight enemies of their deity to protect the world. The Exalted were designed to overthrow the existing deities on behalf of their patrons. The roles of the Exalted is to fundamentally reshape the world; even the 'weak' ones like the terrestrials.<br /> <br /> I don't think a Legacy garou plopped in W5 is going to break the setting. They might disrupt things for a big, but they're mortal, even the strongest can be killed through numbers and attrition, and limited in how big of a scope they can influence by themselves. A Garou has a few decades at best, an Exalted has centuries at worst and can scale up to the power to manipulate continents worth of peoples and countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-16T13:29:27-08:00","id":1558353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558347#post1558347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apples and oranges?<br /> <br /> Garou were designed to fight enemies of their deity to protect the world. The Exalted were designed to overthrow the existing deities on behalf of their patrons. The roles of the Exalted is to fundamentally reshape the world; even the 'weak' ones like the terrestrials.<br /> <br /> I don't think a Legacy garou plopped in W5 is going to break the setting. They might disrupt things for a big, but they're mortal, even the strongest can be killed through numbers and attrition, and limited in how big of a scope they can influence by themselves. A Garou has a few decades at best, an Exalted has centuries at worst and can scale up to the power to manipulate continents worth of peoples and countries.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While we're on the subject of Exalted, there's a bit of obscure lore I'd like some clarification on.<br /> <br /> I've heard that Exalted supposedly takes place as a prequel setting to World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Is that true? Because if it is, then that stirs up a lot of questions regarding the state of WoD's metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-16T16:56:28-08:00","id":1558357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558347#post1558347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apples and oranges?<br /> <br /> Garou were designed to fight enemies of their deity to protect the world. The Exalted were designed to overthrow the existing deities on behalf of their patrons. The roles of the Exalted is to fundamentally reshape the world; even the 'weak' ones like the terrestrials.<br /> <br /> I don't think a Legacy garou plopped in W5 is going to break the setting. They might disrupt things for a big, but they're mortal, even the strongest can be killed through numbers and attrition, and limited in how big of a scope they can influence by themselves. A Garou has a few decades at best, an Exalted has centuries at worst and can scale up to the power to manipulate continents worth of peoples and countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Edit: So closer to a Imbued popping up in H 5 then.<br /> <br /> Though on a unrelated note one thought experiment I was toying around is the presence of a legacy garou could shift W5 metaphysics back to legacy. With the effect growing stronger the longer they survive. I wonder what would be the implications for w5 as a whole...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558353#post1558353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So just a imbued turning up in H5? Good to know though I wonder what would happen if the simple presence of a W20 wolf would slowly bend W5 back into W20 as long as they survive.I wonder what the Concequnces would be?<br /> <br /> While we're on the subject of Exalted, there's a bit of obscure lore I'd like some clarification on.<br /> <br /> I've heard that Exalted supposedly takes place as a prequel setting to World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Is that true? Because if it is, then that stirs up a lot of questions regarding the state of WoD's metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was abandoned in early production as far as I know. Only the Fan Made Exalted vs Wod really explored that premise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 02-16-2026, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-16T22:58:17-08:00","id":1558359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558357#post1558357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was abandoned in early production as far as I know. Only the Fan Made Exalted vs Wod really explored that premise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems you may have cut part of somebody else's quote in that reply, but thanks for the clarification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-16T23:18:19-08:00","id":1558360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558353#post1558353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we're on the subject of Exalted, there's a bit of obscure lore I'd like some clarification on.<br /> <br /> I've heard that Exalted supposedly takes place as a prequel setting to World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Is that true? Because if it is, then that stirs up a lot of questions regarding the state of WoD's metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very early on in the development cycle that was the plan. Some of the earliest advertisements for Exalted and dev interviews were pushing the idea that &quot;before there was a World of Darkness&quot; there was the Exalted setting, and that in terms of the Kote cosmology, Exalted took place back during the Second Age. There was a bit of a pushback and grumbling from the fanbase though and during rewrites this idea was removed, so by the time the corebook released there was no longer any official or canonical links between Exalted and the World of Darkness, just various loose threads, names and some similar concepts. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-17T19:26:27-08:00","id":1558370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558360#post1558360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very early on in the development cycle that was the plan. Some of the earliest advertisements for Exalted and dev interviews were pushing the idea that &quot;before there was a World of Darkness&quot; there was the Exalted setting, and that in terms of the Kote cosmology, Exalted took place back during the Second Age. There was a bit of a pushback and grumbling from the fanbase though and during rewrites this idea was removed, so by the time the corebook released there was no longer any official or canonical links between Exalted and the World of Darkness, just various loose threads, names and some similar concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also the imbued was apparently going to be the modern nights version of the Solars. At least that's what EX vs WoD goes with since solars outright replaced imbued. Granted in relatively Nerfed form alongside all the Celestials so they can't immediately roll over the setting. <br /> <br /> <br /> But back to the main topic of this thread, what would be the effects of the existence of legacy garous in W5 assuming they live long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T03:51:35-07:00","id":1559877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1558370#post1558370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also the imbued was apparently going to be the modern nights version of the Solars. At least that's what EX vs WoD goes with since solars outright replaced imbued. Granted in relatively Nerfed form alongside all the Celestials so they can't immediately roll over the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> But back to the main topic of this thread, what would be the effects of the existence of legacy garous in W5 assuming they live long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that pre-W5 society for the Garou revolved around a might makes right mentality, and pack leaders tended to be the strongest, most brutal members?<br /> <br /> They would either<br /> <br /> A) get kicked out of their pack for being an insufferable ass hole.<br /> <br /> B) Kick the living shit out of their so called 'allies,' until they bent the knee in submission.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the Silver Fangs would be foaming at the mouth upon hearing that not only did the Garou nation collapse, but their tribe has started to accept lowly, fucking, mixed-breed peasants into their holy bloodline.<br /> <br /> Heck, they might just decide to purge their own tribe!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T04:46:24-07:00","id":1559879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559877#post1559877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering that pre-W5 society for the Garou revolved around a might makes right mentality, and pack leaders tended to be the strongest, most brutal members?</div> </div> </div> </div>Drastically over-sold in presentation and unlikely when packs with other priorities than being Grunting Space Marines exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They would either<br /> <br /> A) get kicked out of their pack for being an insufferable ass hole.<br /> <br /> B) Kick the living shit out of their so called 'allies,' until they bent the knee in submission.<br /> <br /> And, of course, the Silver Fangs would be foaming at the mouth upon hearing that not only did the Garou nation collapse, but their tribe has started to accept lowly, fucking, mixed-breed peasants into their holy bloodline.<br /> <br /> Heck, they might just decide to purge their own tribe! </div> </div> </div>The only halfway accurate part of this post involves the Fangs. The ones not in the Renewal Camp, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T05:59:48-07:00","id":1559881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559879#post1559879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Drastically over-sold in presentation and unlikely when packs with other priorities than being Grunting Space Marines exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, the<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia - Pacifists who have forgotten what it is they were specifically created to do.<br /> <br /> Stargazers - Deserters who fucked off to the mountains somewhere and abandoned the war against the Wyrm so they could pursue enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers / Glass Walkers - Traitors who are advocating to help optimize human industrialization efforts, instead of putting a stop to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> But you take a look at the Black Furies, the Red Talons, the Shadow Lords, the Get of Fenris, the Silver Fangs, the Fianna, the Windego and Uktena... what do they all have in common?<br /> <br /> They are warriors, who's approach to problem solving often involves liberal use of extreme violence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559879#post1559879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The only halfway accurate part of this post involves the Fangs. The ones not in the Renewal Camp, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you played Book of Hungry Names?<br /> <br /> Your packmates in the opening prologue are so abusive towards your character, that I almost immediately found myself wishing death upon them.<br /> <br /> First chance I had to ditch them, I kicked the shit out of Scarper, blocked his phone number, and left Eyes of Clay to die in agony. That's what the idiot gets for trying to eat a fucking Bane!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T07:33:39-07:00","id":1559882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559881#post1559881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, yes, the<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia - Pacifists who have forgotten what it is they were specifically created to do.<br /> <br /> Stargazers - Deserters who fucked off to the mountains somewhere and abandoned the war against the Wyrm so they could pursue enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers / Glass Walkers - Traitors who are advocating to help optimize human industrialization efforts, instead of putting a stop to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> But you take a look at the Black Furies, the Red Talons, the Shadow Lords, the Get of Fenris, the Silver Fangs, the Fianna, the Windego and Uktena... what do they all have in common?<br /> <br /> They are warriors, who's approach to problem solving often involves liberal use of extreme violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're leaning into a bizarre take on 1e more than W5 is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Have you played Book of Hungry Names? </div> </div> </div>Have you read any of the books?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your packmates in the opening prologue are so abusive towards your character, that I almost immediately found myself wishing death upon them.<br /> <br /> First chance I had to ditch them, I kicked the shit out of Scarper, blocked his phone number, and left Eyes of Clay to die in agony. That's what the idiot gets for trying to eat a fucking Bane! </div> </div> </div>It's a W5 joint. I wouldn't expect nice things from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T13:50:28-07:00","id":1559888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559882#post1559882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're leaning into a bizarre take on 1e more than W5 is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because this topic is about what would happen if a pre-W5 werewolf suddenly found themselves transported into the W5 setting.<br /> <br /> Also, how is it bizarre? Because this is what I've been told about their previous incarnations.<br /> <br /> <br /> Black Furies - Were so filled with cruelty and hatred towards men, that they scared off not one, but TWO of their original Totems. Their method of reproduction was to abduct a man off the street, and <b>rape him to death.</b> And if the child came out male, they would sacrifice him, because he was seen as inherently evil.<br /> <br /> <br /> Get of Fenris were utterly obsessed with being the strongest warriors they could possibly be, and did not respect anybody who lacked the power to defend themselves from agressors.<br /> <br /> <br /> Silver Fangs considered their bloodline to be sacred, even going so far as to engage in multi generational incest to avoid diluting it. And when they were warned about the consequences of what would happen if they refused to abandon their status after 7 years, they boldly accepted the price. Because they would rather choose a life time of insanity, than relinquish their authority to the lesser tribes.<br /> <br /> They also refused to acknowledge that they were even capable of making a mistake. If such a thing happened, the Silver Fangs would sweep it under the rug and destroy the evidence, so that they would always be seen as perfect, infallible leaders of the Garou nation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shadow Lords - I can't tell you how these guys operate, because anybody who tries to do so has quickly gone missing. But I can say that they were committed to getting the job done.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Uktena - &quot;Let's kill all the white people!&quot;<br /> <br /> Windego - &quot;Let's kill all the white people, and let's eat their flesh!&quot;<br /> <br /> Red Talons - &quot;Let's just kill all the people in general. Men, women, children, doesn't matter. Griffin wants them gone!&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T16:11:28-07:00","id":1559890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559888#post1559888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because this is what I've been told about their previous incarnations.</div> </div> </div> </div>And thus the problem.<br /> <br /> Learning about the Tribes second hand means you have a limited understanding of the Tribes. WtA, over three original editions and W20 (and if you want to appeal to the nature of the thread, the thread is about a W20 Garou moved into W5 which means Tribes that have over a decade of development to be more nuanced and complex cultures) to expand on each of the Tribes and how they work. That's four core books, three players guides, two editions of Tribebooks and a W20 single book for each of the Tribes, broad books that get into individual Tribal variations on things like how they view Auspices or Fetish crafting, and on and on and on.<br /> <br /> All of your takes are, if not bizarre, are superficial and narrow to the point of sounding more like parody than actually trying to represent the setting of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T16:47:59-07:00","id":1559891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559890#post1559890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the thread is about a W20 Garou moved into W5 which means Tribes that have over a decade of development to be more nuanced and complex cultures) to expand on each of the Tribes and how they work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it's still difficult for me to wrap my head around the idea of the 20th anniversary books being seen as their own editions. I thought they were supposed to be a compilation of what had been previously established.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T17:40:31-07:00","id":1559892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559891#post1559891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it's still difficult for me to wrap my head around the idea of the 20th anniversary books being seen as their own editions. I thought they were supposed to be a compilation of what had been previously established.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were. Then Paradox bought the IP to make a game that they couldn't and put the PnP side in charge of people with very narrow views on the setting, to a point that, much as Heavy Arms noted, it's more of a parody of existing material than a &quot;fresh, 21st century&quot; take on the subject.<br /> <br /> That's why Changing Ways became utterly terrible. Instead of addressing the gradual mission creep of the 20th Anniversary editions as actual editions and expanding W20, it made W20 more superficial due to editorial bias. The Vampire mains in charge of V5 pretty much cut everything from every other game off at the knees so that they would be superficial self-parodies compared to prior editions of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T19:19:43-07:00","id":1559894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559892#post1559892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were. Then Paradox bought the IP to make a game that they couldn't and put the PnP side in charge of people with very narrow views on the setting, to a point that, much as Heavy Arms noted, it's more of a parody of existing material than a &quot;fresh, 21st century&quot; take on the subject.<br /> <br /> That's why Changing Ways became utterly terrible. Instead of addressing the gradual mission creep of the 20th Anniversary editions as actual editions and expanding W20, it made W20 more superficial due to editorial bias. The Vampire mains in charge of V5 pretty much cut everything from every other game off at the knees so that they would be superficial self-parodies compared to prior editions of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's just downright disappointing!<br /> <br /> Maybe Paradox should stick to producing strategy games, and leave the more in depth role playing stuff to people who actually know what they're doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-11T22:22:52-07:00","id":1559896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559894#post1559894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's just downright disappointing!<br /> <br /> Maybe Paradox should stick to producing strategy games, and leave the more in depth role playing stuff to people who actually know what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>They already don't care. They delegated the PnP stuff to the people they deemed qualified to do so, who then made that infamous press conference, shaved everything from Vampire off to follow their One True Way, started an international incident due to bad editing, got the WW under Paradox dissolved, and now are writing for a remade WW spun off so that Paradox could sell the IP if Bloodlines 2 didn't pan out. And, since BL2 did, indeed, underperform, has an uncertain future except in one regard: the PnP business is something that PDX does not care about at all and has little to no bearing on whoever shows up with enough money to buy it from PDX.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T00:48:03-07:00","id":1559897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559896#post1559896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They already don't care. They delegated the PnP stuff to the people they deemed qualified to do so, who then made that infamous press conference, shaved everything from Vampire off to follow their One True Way, started an international incident due to bad editing, got the WW under Paradox dissolved, and now are writing for a remade WW spun off so that Paradox could sell the IP if Bloodlines 2 didn't pan out. And, since BL2 did, indeed, underperform, has an uncertain future except in one regard: the PnP business is something that PDX does not care about at all and has little to no bearing on whoever shows up with enough money to buy it from PDX.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of which, we're getting a new Werewolf game: <b>Rageborn</b><br /> <br /> W:tA meets V Rising. I suppose it can't be any worse than <b>Earthblood</b>...<br /> <br /> Please don't be worse than <b>Earthblood.</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T06:41:07-07:00","id":1559899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559894#post1559894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's just downright disappointing!<br /> <br /> Maybe Paradox should stick to producing strategy games, and leave the more in depth role playing stuff to people who actually know what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox doesn't care and the whole book-side of things has been a mismanaged mess for ages. Even right now, you have Renegade put out supplements for WOD5E - but it's not like Renegade really has full control over this. Renegade isn't able to put out something like a M5 corebook, for example. At the same time, the newly (re-)established White Wolf aren't the ones developing the supplements at the moment either. That's what Renegade does. Even though Paradox wanted to do its &quot;One True Way&quot;-approach by focusing on 5th edition, the way 5th edition books are developed and by whom has been changing constantly over the years. It's also has been a chaotic mess most of the time where it's quite tricky to explain who was doing what when. And it's bound to change again if they're really trying to go with the &quot;Everything will be done in-house by White Wolf alone&quot;-approach. The whole process has been a mismanaged mess and even if they eventually do everything in-house with the resurrected White Wolf, give it a year or two and I bet Paradox will have changed its mind yet again on how the whole thing is organised. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Speaking of which, we're getting a new Werewolf game: Rageborn<br /> <br /> W:tA meets V Rising. I suppose it can't be any worse than Earthblood...<br /> <br /> Please don't be worse than Earthblood. </div> </div> </div>According to the description, it's a top-down Metroidvania-type of game. So it's more in line with stuff like &quot;Hollow Knight&quot; or &quot;Ori and the Blind Forest&quot; with a bit more focus on combat, I guess. At least that's my impression from what was shown and was said about the game. <br /> <br /> But this game has the same issue that the Hunter: Deathwish game has. It's published by Nacon - which are currently undergoing an insolvency-procedure. Luckily, neither studio is owned by Nacon directly or they would become part of this mess. But I hope Paradox has a plan B in case things go catastrophically wrong with Nacon. For example, just a few days ago, we've got a report saying &quot;Nacon Puts Midgar Studio Up for Sale One Day After Spotlighting Its RPG Edge of Memories at Nacon Connect 2026&quot; (<a href=\"https://wccftech.com/nacon-puts-edge-of-memories-midgar-studio-up-for-sale-amidst-insolvency-crisis/\" target=\"_blank\">source</a>). They announced a game called Edge of Memories on that same show that previewed Rageborn as well and now they're putting up the studio for sale as Nacon are scrambling to get through this insolvency-procedure. That's not a good sign, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T10:48:33-07:00","id":1559902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559899#post1559899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> According to the description, it's a top-down Metroidvania-type of game. So it's more in line with stuff like &quot;Hollow Knight&quot; or &quot;Ori and the Blind Forest&quot; with a bit more focus on combat, I guess. At least that's my impression from what was shown and was said about the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they meant in terms of visual aesthetics. I just looked up their announcement video and it does indeed look very similar to V Rising, minus the base building mechanic.<br /> <br /> Not that that's necessarily a bad thing, as V Rising was a fairly popular game for a while.<br /> <br /> I wonder what tribe we'll be playing as?<br /> <br /> Similarly, I wonder if the devs even know how the tribes are supposed to function?<br /> <br /> Because Cahal was the least Fianna-y Fianna to ever Fianna!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T11:31:38-07:00","id":1559903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559902#post1559902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they meant in terms of visual aesthetics. I just looked up their announcement video and it does indeed look very similar to V Rising, minus the base building mechanic.<br /> <br /> Not that that's necessarily a bad thing, as V Rising was a fairly popular game for a while.<br /> <br /> I wonder what tribe we'll be playing as?<br /> <br /> Similarly, I wonder if the devs even know how the tribes are supposed to function?<br /> <br /> Because Cahal was the least Fianna-y Fianna to ever Fianna!</div> </div> </div> </div>What I was referring to was them saying on the steam-page &quot;Master three forms of the Garou, explore the wilds of Alaska, and confront the Wyrm in this visceral action-adventure metroidvania.&quot;<br /> <br /> Always possible that it turns out to be inaccurate once we get to see more of the game but they're calling it a Metroidvania-style game. <br /> <br /> As far as being faithful to WtA is concerned... Them mentioning only three Forms is concerning but I could imagine that following the Metroidvania-tropes Glabro and Hispo might end up being unlockable Forms as they give abilities which allow you to enter new areas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T12:11:45-07:00","id":1559904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559902#post1559902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think they meant in terms of visual aesthetics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's what the gameplay footage immediately made me think of.<br /> <br /> ---------------------<br /> <br /> I think you're right, Knightingale. They were using Lupus form to air dash across platforms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T17:11:58-07:00","id":1559906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559903#post1559903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I was referring to was them saying on the steam-page &quot;Master three forms of the Garou, explore the wilds of Alaska, and confront the Wyrm in this visceral action-adventure metroidvania.&quot;<br /> <br /> Always possible that it turns out to be inaccurate once we get to see more of the game but they're calling it a Metroidvania-style game.<br /> <br /> As far as being faithful to WtA is concerned... Them mentioning only three Forms is concerning but I could imagine that following the Metroidvania-tropes Glabro and Hispo might end up being unlockable Forms as they give abilities which allow you to enter new areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a shame that everyone's drunk on the &quot;Crinos is the endgame form&quot; and never bothered to look at the Charms that tweaked it. <a href=\"https://www.wyrmfoe.com/1466/invocation-of-the-pharaoh/\" target=\"_blank\">Invocation of the Pharaoh</a> would probably get the Silent Striders no end of fans while also styling on the &quot;Garou get no social effects!&quot; crowd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T19:41:54-07:00","id":1559908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559894#post1559894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that's just downright disappointing!<br /> <br /> Maybe Paradox should stick to producing strategy games, and leave the more in depth role playing stuff to people who actually know what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well to in addition there's also a LARP focused version of WTA by a company called Minds Eye Theater that also has some major lore changes like a apocalypse already happened which as a killed off most of the old Metaplot Characters and blew up most of the Cearns.<br /> <br /> As a consequence of that the garou nation was split into two opposing tribal alliances which roughly maps to conservative and progressive and some major reorganization of the tribe (An example would be a the stargezers basically becoming a Children of gaia camp). Finally there's also the emergence of the Bitten which is basically kinfolk transformed into a garou via bite of another garou, they have some stigma attached to them for various resions, such the fact they're sterile, so they can't breed more garous and the fact that most bitten is a result of the BSD version of the shovel heads.<br /> <br /> Apparently a previous version of W5 was going to use MET lore as a base before being cancelled. With At least one of the former writers (J. F. Sambrano) leaving on less than favorable tyerms. He's currently on his own orginal werewolf game called Extinction: the Fate of Mongrels and another Fan book called werewolf the Essentials that also uses BNS lore as a base.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559903#post1559903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I was referring to was them saying on the steam-page &quot;Master three forms of the Garou, explore the wilds of Alaska, and confront the Wyrm in this visceral action-adventure metroidvania.&quot;<br /> <br /> Always possible that it turns out to be inaccurate once we get to see more of the game but they're calling it a Metroidvania-style game.<br /> <br /> As far as being faithful to WtA is concerned... Them mentioning only three Forms is concerning but I could imagine that following the Metroidvania-tropes Glabro and Hispo might end up being unlockable Forms as they give abilities which allow you to enter new areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that the trailer shows a Hispo since the one shot of the wolf was visablly larger. Also this is the second time I saw a metoridvaina starring a werewolf with -born in the name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=piRiB7kxR9M\" data-code=\"piRiB7kxR9M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/piRiB7kxR9M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25848,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","user":"MrornX","date":". 05-12-2026, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T20:53:46-07:00","id":1559909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559908#post1559908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally there's also the emergence of the Bitten which is basically kinfolk transformed into a garou via bite of another garou, they have some stigma attached to them for various resions, such the fact they're sterile, so they can't breed more garous and the fact that most bitten is a result of the BSD version of the shovel heads.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn it, they almost fixed the RNG transformation mechanic, but then had to go and add sterility to it.<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of the classic mythology, where lycanthropy can be transmitted like a disease or a curse. Having it be turned into a spiritual calling that strikes totally random people irritates me.<br /> <br /> If I had a say in the matter, the Fera would be spreading the Changing Seed like wildfire. If they can't genocide humanity, maybe they can assimilate it instead!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559908#post1559908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also this is the second time I saw a metoridvaina starring a werewolf with -born in the name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=piRiB7kxR9M\" data-code=\"piRiB7kxR9M\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/piRiB7kxR9M/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T00:02:54-07:00","id":1559910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559909#post1559909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Damn it, they almost fixed the RNG transformation mechanic, but then had to go and add sterility to it.<br /> <br /> I'm a fan of the classic mythology, where lycanthropy can be transmitted like a disease or a curse. Having it be turned into a spiritual calling that strikes totally random people irritates me.<br /> <br /> If I had a say in the matter, the Fera would be spreading the Changing Seed like wildfire. If they can't genocide humanity, maybe they can assimilate it instead!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There's no problems with your liking it, but there's a huge-ass problem with misrepresenting Hollywood constructions as old, mythological legendry and trying to establish it as more legit than any other tales. Of which there are a dizzying variety just from actual classic (Greek) myth, where the curse is usually unique but there's also ritual anthopophagy that can turn participants into a wolf for nine years, or permanently if they eat human flesh as a wolf. That is, of course, from myths where Zeus doesn't just insta-kill King Lycaon or his sons for their perfidy instead of cursing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T00:13:41-07:00","id":1559911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559910#post1559910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no problems with your liking it, but there's a huge-ass problem with misrepresenting Hollywood constructions as old, mythological legendry and trying to establish it as more legit than any other tales. Of which there are a dizzying variety just from actual classic (Greek) myth, where the curse is usually unique but there's also ritual anthopophagy that can turn participants into a wolf for nine years, or permanently if they eat human flesh as a wolf. That is, of course, from myths where Zeus doesn't just insta-kill King Lycaon or his sons for their perfidy instead of cursing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also skinwalker witches.<br /> <br /> You can become a werewolf if you drink rain water out of a wolf's pawprint.<br /> <br /> There's an old Russian spell that requires a pure copper knife to perform.<br /> <br /> But I agree with Ratkin that the bite transmission has just become iconic at this point.<br /> <br /> Messing with it feels weird. Like, imagine if instead of being embraced by another vampire, you became kindred after committing suicide, or because you received an improper burial. Or maybe you have red hair and blue eyes, you were the last to be born of 7 sons, or you were previously a werewolf when you lived.<br /> <br /> All of these are potential methods for becoming a vampire throughout the world's folklore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T00:42:34-07:00","id":1559912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559909#post1559909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a fan of the classic mythology, where lycanthropy can be transmitted like a disease or a curse. Having it be turned into a spiritual calling that strikes totally random people irritates me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there is Forsaken homebrew called<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1dr9klFe1InGiCGWHT22BmweFrMyBhQ3py2lbCMk-ImE/edit?pli=1&amp;tab=t.0#heading=h.2u5urnjdticv\" target=\"_blank\"> werewolf the cursed</a> that close to what you want.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559909#post1559909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had a say in the matter, the Fera would be spreading the Changing Seed like wildfire. If they can't genocide humanity, maybe they can assimilate it instead!</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of a rework of the breeds where werewolves could actually breed true, though the resulting pup tend to grow up with some issues because they can't really get a normal child hood due to a combination of being born in warfrom and the current state of Garou society, so the best could get is a totally isolated on compound with other pups to keep them company or nonstop training for the war as soon as they could walk.<br /> <br /> Add to that they're fertility is slowly decreasing with the modern nights being at historical lows with the sliver fangs being the most adversely effected. Which is bad for them since traditionally the king should be pure blooded garou not a kinborn which is why a normal kinborn like Albrict ascension to the role would cause a great amount of controversy.<br /> <br /> Also the canon War/Crinosrborn is actually a result of Lupine and humanoid mating and the releviant line in the lantry is changed from no mating period to Don't do Bestiality. Though recently there's rumors crinosborn are born from garou pairing which lead to some panic from the greater nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T00:55:21-07:00","id":1559913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559912#post1559912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also the canon War/Crinosrborn is actually a result of Lupine and humanoid mating and the releviant line in the lantry is changed from no mating period to Don't do Bestiality. Though recently there's rumors crinosborn are born from garou pairing which lead to some panic from the greater nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but there in is a logical paradox.<br /> <br /> Garou are neither human, nor wolf, but something in between.<br /> <br /> If rejecting their human side is bad, then rejecting their animal side should be as well.<br /> <br /> Plus, is it really bestiality, if the lupus born is capable of passing the Harkness test?<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, they were originally born an animal. But the First Change granted them sapience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T01:00:52-07:00","id":1559915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559913#post1559913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus, is it really bestiality, if the lupus born is capable of passing the Harkness test?<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, they were originally born an animal. But the First Change granted them sapience.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's how you start a debate about a shapeshifting druid having sex in bear form. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T01:06:01-07:00","id":1559916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559910#post1559910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no problems with your liking it, but there's a huge-ass problem with misrepresenting Hollywood constructions as old, mythological legendry and trying to establish it as more legit than any other tales. Of which there are a dizzying variety just from actual classic (Greek) myth, where the curse is usually unique but there's also ritual anthopophagy that can turn participants into a wolf for nine years, or permanently if they eat human flesh as a wolf. That is, of course, from myths where Zeus doesn't just insta-kill King Lycaon or his sons for their perfidy instead of cursing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm getting really tired of people trying to lecture me about how the pop culture media interpretation of various myths isn't 100% accurate, or the only take on the subject.<br /> <br /> I'm fully aware of that; but when I mention the term &quot;werewolf&quot; around people, they usually have an intuitive understanding of what kind of werewolf I'm talking about. The infection version is by far the most iconic, while any other type of werewolf is more esoteric, or niche community knowledge.<br /> <br /> It's 2026; you can stop virtue signaling now, nobody cares anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T04:26:51-07:00","id":1559919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559915#post1559915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's how you start a debate about a shapeshifting druid having sex in bear form. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>More than a year later, and people were still arguing over that on Steam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T11:19:55-07:00","id":1559927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559916#post1559916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm getting really tired of people trying to lecture me about how the pop culture media interpretation of various myths isn't 100% accurate, or the only take on the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stop digging up cold, shit takes from 1996, then.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm fully aware of that; but when I mention the term &quot;werewolf&quot; around people, they usually have an intuitive understanding of what kind of werewolf I'm talking about. The infection version is by far the most iconic, while any other type of werewolf is more esoteric, or niche community knowledge.<br /> <br /> It's 2026; you can stop virtue signaling now, nobody cares anymore. </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's 2026. I've been in this fandom for 30 years now and the Angst Parade has never let up in that time with its &quot;I think that this game would be better if it were more like Vampire&quot; BS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T12:59:59-07:00","id":1559930,"title":"","content":"There's also some serious confirmation bias that always happens when this comes up. Horror fans see &quot;bite transferred curse&quot; as iconic in ways more general audiences frequently don't. Urban fantasy fans (esp. the romance heavy side of it) are used to much bigger moves away from <i>The Wolfman </i> and <i>An American Werewolf in London</i>. And it's really simple why this happens: &quot;I'm a normal human except on full moons I transform into an uncontrollable beast&quot; doesn't work in most genres. The &quot;alpha wolf&quot; trope is far more iconic in pop culture werewolves because it's actually useful in multiple genres as a basis for werewolf social groups that operate differently from human society.<br /> <br /> And, of course, most pop culture doesn't have a need to draw hard lines between werewolf and vampire. <i>Teen Wolf</i> was a pretty popular 2010s show that stuck to the &quot;bitten&quot; take, but that aspect fades into the background pretty fast to look far more like something most WoD fans would consider VtM territory (ex: where the wolf that bit you sits on the &quot;alpha&quot; hierarchy puts expectations on new werewolves regarding local politics; if you're bitten by an Alpha like the main character was, you're expected to become one yourself and people are going to treat you that way).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T13:48:48-07:00","id":1559931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559930#post1559930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, of course, most pop culture doesn't have a need to draw hard lines between werewolf and vampire. <i>Teen Wolf</i> was a pretty popular 2010s show that stuck to the &quot;bitten&quot; take, but that aspect fades into the background pretty fast to look far more like something most WoD fans would consider VtM territory (ex: where the wolf that bit you sits on the &quot;alpha&quot; hierarchy puts expectations on new werewolves regarding local politics; if you're bitten by an Alpha like the main character was, you're expected to become one yourself and people are going to treat you that way).</div> </div> </div> </div>Teen Wolf confused me. I thought it was a movie, but turns out it was a TV show. And for some reason, the villain went full Crinos form during the full moon, while the protagonist went Glabro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T14:03:57-07:00","id":1559932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559927#post1559927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop digging up cold, shit takes from 1996, then.</div> </div> </div> </div>My shit takes are the best shit takes!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559927#post1559927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, it's 2026. I've been in this fandom for 30 years now and the Angst Parade has never let up in that time with its &quot;I think that this game would be better if it were more like Vampire&quot; BS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who said anything about angst? I just don't like seeing the supernatural population being driven to gradual extinction by God's little vanity project (humanity).<br /> <br /> Magic is a gift. Magic is power. Magic is freedom. And I like to see it be more readily accessible, than going decades of your life hoping that you finally win the cosmic lottery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T14:04:45-07:00","id":1559933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559930#post1559930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also some serious confirmation bias that always happens when this comes up. Horror fans see &quot;bite transferred curse&quot; as iconic in ways more general audiences frequently don't. Urban fantasy fans (esp. the romance heavy side of it) are used to much bigger moves away from <i>The Wolfman </i> and <i>An American Werewolf in London</i>. And it's really simple why this happens: &quot;I'm a normal human except on full moons I transform into an uncontrollable beast&quot; doesn't work in most genres. The &quot;alpha wolf&quot; trope is far more iconic in pop culture werewolves because it's actually useful in multiple genres as a basis for werewolf social groups that operate differently from human society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Being Human - Both the American and British versions.<br /> <br /> Teen Wolf<br /> <br /> Project Metal Beast<br /> <br /> Underworld<br /> <br /> Cursed<br /> <br /> Bitten -Well, obviously, it's in the name<br /> <br /> D&amp;D / Pathfinder<br /> <br /> Elder Scrolls<br /> <br /> Fable<br /> <br /> The Wolfman<br /> <br /> Van Hellsing<br /> <br /> The list of stories that pass it on through bites just kind of keeps going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T15:22:11-07:00","id":1559935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559931#post1559931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was a movie, but turns out it was a TV show.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's both, as it's one big franchise however disconnected. There was a 1985 movie (which had a sequel), an '80s cartoon, and 2011 TV show, and a movie based on the '11 TV show as well.<br /> <br /> The '11 show was originally meant to be an adaptation of the '85 movie, but kinda went off those rails pretty fast just like Riverdale and it looking anything like Archie from the old comics.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559933#post1559933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The list of stories that pass it on through bites just kind of keeps going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, 11 examples over 85 years. Very impressive.<br /> <br /> Though less sarcastically, that's just making my point about confirmation bias. You're not looking at all werewolf media (an impossible task to do realistically) even over any set period of time. You're not even trying to make a case on cultural impact in response to a post about pop-culture presence of certain tropes/elements. <br /> <br /> While I'm prepared for people to post all sorts of shit for bringing this up it's part of the problem:<br /> <br /> The Twilight series.<br /> <br /> In broad pop culture how many people can name Jacob as a famous fictional werewolf character vs. specific characters from any of those (even if Twilight fans will probably &quot;well actually...&quot; to no end because Jacob is a shape-shifter and those are different from werewolves in the Twilight setting even if Jacob is from a line of shape-shifters that can only turn into wolves). How many people think how Jacob's version of being a werewolf is how things work vs. any of those specific examples?<br /> <br /> 'Cause Jacob?<br /> <br /> Got his powers via birth into the right family.<br /> His family, and others like them, got their powers from animist spirits (and is explicitly Native American at that).<br /> Voluntary shape-shifting.<br /> Enhanced healing, physical prowess, and senses without needing to shift; leading to much longer potential life-span if they don't die in feuds with other supernaturals.<br /> Alpha wolf trope present (you didn't even bother listing how much that comes up in your own examples).<br /> Packs develop telepathic communication.<br /> <br /> So is that immensely popular franchise's depiction of it's main wolf character something that sounds like any of your examples, or sounds like someone putting their WtA PC into another project?<br /> <br /> Because even if you think Twilight is hot garbage, it was very, very popular, and a lot of people are going to see Jacob as a &quot;normal&quot; style werewolf because it was just that big as a franchise. People that have probably never heard of things like Project Metal Beast or Cursed (those are some pretty niche picks).<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about iconic, you can't just rattle off a list of stories, because you're making cultural influence and impact part of the evaluation. It doesn't matter if there's ten &quot;bitten&quot; stories for every other type of werewolf story, if the other type of werewolf story has a billion dollar franchise attached to it and most of the bitten stories are cult classics or niche films only horror genre fans care about.<br /> <br /> It also matters a lot how much &quot;transmission&quot; even matters to a given story. Like, a gigantic plot point of the Underworld franchise is that there's a combination of exposure to the different strains of the virus and genetics of those descending from the mortal son of the Corvinus family. Biting isn't even important because it's just a blood borne virus that can be transmitted in multiple ways (Lucian was the start of a whole second type of werewolf as the virus mutated from his mother to him during pregnancy, so he was never bitten to become one). So the bite is there, but it's really not what matters to the story and that the bite is simply one of many transmission vectors is very plot relevant. This is completely different from the Being Human series where the whole any normal human can become a werewolf by being bitten is a more central part of the drama for the werewolf character trying to navigate their human life, their flat/house mates, and the wider supernatural world were werewolves aren't really organized because they're more incidental compared to groups like vampires.<br /> <br /> And then there's points like should D&amp;D, TES, Fable, or Van Hellsing even count because they're not stories about werewolves directly, they're broad fantasy stories that happen to have werewolves in them (and some of them are playable to an extent for the games). You can run D&amp;D and never deal with a werewolf. TES and Fable (if they even come up in a given game) engaging with werewolves is largely optional and getting infected is made fairly simple to deal with if you don't want to play one; it's basically just a disease that any magical disease cure can get rid of (if on a timer). Etc.<br /> <br /> So... yeah, a list doesn't mean much, because it's not actually making a point. You didn't pull a mic drop, you showed off how little you care to engage in your own point's logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T16:09:30-07:00","id":1559936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559932#post1559932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My shit takes are the best shit takes!<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It was acceptable in the 90s<br /> <br /> It was acceptable at the time!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who said anything about angst? I just don't like seeing the supernatural population being driven to gradual extinction by God's little vanity project (humanity).<br /> <br /> Magic is a gift. Magic is power. Magic is freedom. And I like to see it be more readily accessible, than going decades of your life hoping that you finally win the cosmic lottery. </div> </div> </div>The theme of the game involves a serious concern over extinction. Making the werewolves in no danger of it would be much closer to being a completely indulgent power fantasy where you do whatever and bemoan your personal problems at having, as you put it, &quot;a gift, power, freedom&quot; but having to deal with &quot;the normies&quot;. It also ropes in cycles of violence with Garou openly brutalizing humanity and laying claim to populations of them back in the earliest days of settlement-founding, then relenting but not as well as they potentially could have.<br /> <br /> (Also, if you wanted to talk about humanity created by god... you're in the wrong forum. You want Vampire, or the general WoD with a Demon flair.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T16:50:48-07:00","id":1559937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559935#post1559935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Twilight series.<br /> <br /> In broad pop culture how many people can name Jacob as a famous fictional werewolf character vs. specific characters from any of those (even if Twilight fans will probably &quot;well actually...&quot; to no end because Jacob is a shape-shifter and those are different from werewolves in the Twilight setting even if Jacob is from a line of shape-shifters that can only turn into wolves). How many people think how Jacob's version of being a werewolf is how things work vs. any of those specific examples?<br /> <br /> 'Cause Jacob?<br /> <br /> Got his powers via birth into the right family.<br /> His family, and others like them, got their powers from animist spirits (and is explicitly Native American at that).<br /> Voluntary shape-shifting.<br /> Enhanced healing, physical prowess, and senses without needing to shift; leading to much longer potential life-span if they don't die in feuds with other supernaturals.<br /> Alpha wolf trope present (you didn't even bother listing how much that comes up in your own examples).<br /> Packs develop telepathic communication.<br /> <br /> So is that immensely popular franchise's depiction of it's main wolf character something that sounds like any of your examples, or sounds like someone putting their WtA PC into another project?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you really going to use the series that portrays child groomers as the protagonists as an example of popular werewolf media?<br /> <br /> And yes, he is a groomer. Because he took one look at a literal newborn infant, and immediately received a vision that she was destined to be his soul mate.<br /> <br /> Like, dude, by the time she's old enough to even consider dating, you're gonna be in your late 30's.<br /> <br /> Good thing Bella's dad is a cop!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T20:09:15-07:00","id":1559941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559937#post1559937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you really going to use the series that portrays child groomers as the protagonists as an example of popular werewolf media?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because it is. I think it's trash, but it's popular trash. Jacob is a shitstain of a person... from an immensely popular supernatural drama series that has had a huge impact of popular ideas of supernatural characters. You can hate it, but you can't deny the book and ticket sales. <br /> <br /> And exactly as I predicted when I said, &quot;While I'm prepared for people to post all sorts of shit for bringing this up it's part of the problem:&quot; in part you didn't quote, you're not actually addressing the point (what pop culture werewolves actually are when you look at pop culture, not just horror genre fan picks) you're bringing up how badly executed a character is.<br /> <br /> I think the Potter-verse is full of trash characters and was created by a trash person... but I'm never going to argue that its popularity is meaningless to pop-culture ideas around urban fantasy magic use, then point to something something like The Lord of Illusions as evidence of what popular magic users look like simply because that movie exists. If you want to talk about what's &quot;iconic&quot; in pop culture, the big franchises always have to be given heavy consideration even if everyone in the conversation agrees they're horrible as art goes, because that's not what &quot;iconic&quot; or &quot;popular&quot; or &quot;influential&quot; means.<br /> <br /> At the risk of another bit of hornet nest stirring: look up the Karma Houdini and Protagonist-Centered Morality pages on TVTropes. The sheer volume of examples of (esp. in the second) of characters getting away with stuff the audience would never tolerate in real life when it comes to fiction is immense and extends far beyond one franchise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T21:55:42-07:00","id":1559943,"title":"","content":"At any rate, it seems we've gotten very much sidetracked. So, in an effort to try focusing back on the OP's post.<br /> <br /> I think a W20 werewolf being informed that Gaia was already dead, and that the Apocalypse was actively happening around them would probably cause them to act out even more psychotically than they already did.<br /> <br /> Hell, that might be the final straw that convinces the Garou Nation to once again reinstate the Impergium. Because of the Apocalypse has begun, then you really have nothing left to lose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T22:08:37-07:00","id":1559944,"title":"","content":"You misunderstand. It's not the frequency with which W:tA are able to shapeshift, nor their powersets that I have a problem with. My comment was specifically directed towards their method of transmission.<br /> <br /> Maybe it's because I have furry bias, but I want more Fera. All the Fera. As many Fera as you can fit on board.<br /> <br /> Humanity has become an evolutionary dead end; and if it will not renew its connection to nature willingly, then they must be forced to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> I wonder if the Ratkin can mass produce the metamorphic plague? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29027,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","user":"GreatHornedRatkin","date":". 05-14-2026, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T23:04:43-07:00","id":1559948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559943#post1559943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At any rate, it seems we've gotten very much sidetracked. So, in an effort to try focusing back on the OP's post.<br /> <br /> I think a W20 werewolf being informed that Gaia was already dead, and that the Apocalypse was actively happening around them would probably cause them to act out even more psychotically than they already did.<br /> <br /> Hell, that might be the final straw that convinces the Garou Nation to once again reinstate the Impergium. Because of the Apocalypse has begun, then you really have nothing left to lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like the premise of a certain Tracy Morgan song, the thread was sweaty from the start. The power of the Wyld refreshed it into something new via thread drift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand. It's not the frequency with which W:tA are able to shapeshift, nor their powersets that I have a problem with. My comment was specifically directed towards their method of transmission.</div> </div> </div> </div>...I don't think anyone misunderstood that. It was quite clear from the outset.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it's because I have furry bias, but I want more Fera. All the Fera. As many Fera as you can fit on board. </div> </div> </div>And you can play them in your own game!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity has become an evolutionary dead end; </div> </div> </div>Shit like that's only determined in hindsight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and if it will not renew its connection to nature willingly, then they must be forced to do so. </div> </div> </div>And that didn't work out so well the first time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder if the Ratkin can mass produce the metamorphic plague? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>That... only ever affected the Black Furies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T00:06:29-07:00","id":1559949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559944#post1559944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstand. It's not the frequency with which W:tA are able to shapeshift, nor their powersets that I have a problem with. My comment was specifically directed towards their method of transmission.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't misunderstand, I reject your attempt to justify a matter of taste as more than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe it's because I have furry bias, but I want more Fera. All the Fera. As many Fera as you can fit on board. </div> </div> </div>Maybe WtA isn't the right game for your desires? Besides the fact that method of transmission is a completely separate issue from wanting more Fera, the idea of the WoD as a setting were the supernatural is mostly kept secret doesn't work if you keep stuffing it with more and more types of critters. There's a reason why the end of 2e and Rev WoD had backlash at how crowded the WoD was getting as it strained the idea that &quot;our world but darker&quot; was sustainable with so many supernaturals in the setting.<br /> <br /> It sounds like what you want is a well executed version of the CofD 1e dud Changing Breeds where all of that side-splat can be shifters of whatever animal types the player(s) want and don't have the baggage of either the Garou/Fera's spirit hierarchy or the inherited duties of the Uratha.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity has become an evolutionary dead end; and if it will not renew its connection to nature willingly, then they must be forced to do so. </div> </div> </div>That's a fairly difficult to justify position since it doesn't really work with how evolution works. A species isn't a &quot;dead end&quot; until it's dead and nothing evolved from it. Evolution doesn't care about a connection to nature; and an appeal to the concept is fairly meaningless as &quot;nature&quot; in this context can mean whatever the speaker wants it to mean instead of an actual discussion of how nature works in a more methodological naturalist sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wonder if the Ratkin can mass produce the metamorphic plague? </div> </div> </div>You don't really mass produce a plague. The issue is if the Ratkin can figure out the best time to spread the plague to get the maximum impact for their goals (and that means they would need sufficiently agreed upon goals which they're not the best at doing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T00:28:11-07:00","id":1559950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559949#post1559949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't misunderstand, I reject your attempt to justify a matter of taste as more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I explicitly said that it was my preference<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559949#post1559949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe WtA isn't the right game for your desires? Besides the fact that method of transmission is a completely separate issue from wanting more Fera, the idea of the WoD as a setting were the supernatural is mostly kept secret doesn't work if you keep stuffing it with more and more types of critters. There's a reason why the end of 2e and Rev WoD had backlash at how crowded the WoD was getting as it strained the idea that &quot;our world but darker&quot; was sustainable with so many supernaturals in the setting.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You keep it a secret until the Times of Judgement / End Times scenario.<br /> <br /> Then you flip the script and go loud.<br /> <br /> Now, remind me, what event is currently happening within the timeframe of 5th edition?<br /> <br /> Oh, that's right. Gehenna / Apocalypse!<br /> <br /> The Antedeluvians are awake, they've put out the call to war, and the masquerade is hanging by a thread after the rise of the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Gaia is dead, the Garou Nation has fallen, and the tribes are running around like headless chickens, with no real plan on what to do next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559949#post1559949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like what you want is a well executed version of the CofD 1e dud Changing Breeds where all of that side-splat can be shifters of whatever animal types the player(s) want and don't have the baggage of either the Garou/Fera's spirit hierarchy or the inherited duties of the Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. I've got no problem with their role or duties within the game's cosmology. I simply want propagating their species to be an easier process than gacha gambling.<br /> <br /> A shame that the Skindancer ritual is accompanied by an automatic point of Wyrm Taint, or we could declare open season on the BSD's.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559949#post1559949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a fairly difficult to justify position since it doesn't really work with how evolution works. A species isn't a &quot;dead end&quot; until it's dead and nothing evolved from it. Evolution doesn't care about a connection to nature; and an appeal to the concept is fairly meaningless as &quot;nature&quot; in this context can mean whatever the speaker wants it to mean instead of an actual discussion of how nature works in a more methodological naturalist sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>*Laughs in Weaver Ascended scenario.* - You know, the one where the deific spirit responsible for humanity's progress all these millennia decides to freeze the planet in eternal stasis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559949#post1559949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You don't really mass produce a plague. The issue is if the Ratkin can figure out the best time to spread the plague to get the maximum impact for their goals (and that means they would need sufficiently agreed upon goals which they're not the best at doing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm aware they're crazy enough to give the Red Talons cause for concern. But somebody ran the math on here a while ago, and determined that there should be enough Ratkin around the globe to carry out Vermintide.\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T04:18:19-07:00","id":1559954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559944#post1559944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559949#post1559949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>All this talk about how werewolves actually breed reminds me of J. F. Sambrano own in progress Not-WtA game where he has a whopping six way his version of the garou could be created called Lineages which manically takes the place of the breeds (and apprently are somewhat compatible with W5). <br /> <br /> The he even wrote some lore for two Lineages which are Born Crying which is classic werewolf by birth and Curse-wrought which are mages who accidentally or purposefully turned them selves into a werewolf via magic. <br /> <br /> The other four are Clan-bound, Pelt-thieves, Spirit-crowned, and Wound-favored.<br /> <br /> You could read more about them on his <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/c/jfsambrano/posts\" target=\"_blank\">Patron </a>for free since the post dosen't have a pay wall last I checked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T05:40:27-07:00","id":1559956,"title":"","content":"All that talk of werewolf-myths remind me of that one W5 adventure called Red Tundra. Because at one point you can go to a pack of wolves and the adventure explains that you're supposed to have a discussion with the leader of this Pack (like actually expecting the player to roll Charisma + Persuasion or Manipulation + Etiquette). Completely normal wolves but somehow their growling translates to a human-like language. They even have names that they gave each other. Very strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T06:31:57-07:00","id":1559957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559956#post1559956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that talk of werewolf-myths remind me of that one W5 adventure called Red Tundra. Because at one point you can go to a pack of wolves and the adventure explains that you're supposed to have a discussion with the leader of this Pack (like actually expecting the player to roll Charisma + Persuasion or Manipulation + Etiquette). Completely normal wolves but somehow their growling translates to a human-like language. They even have names that they gave each other. Very strange.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Reminds of In one of the WTE preview outright said normal wolves are sapient. It just that they have way different thought process to humans but they could quickly learn how to think like us it given the right circumstances. It just that garous have a easier time being human due to the fact they could shape shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T10:34:12-07:00","id":1559959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559956#post1559956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that talk of werewolf-myths remind me of that one W5 adventure called Red Tundra. Because at one point you can go to a pack of wolves and the adventure explains that you're supposed to have a discussion with the leader of this Pack (like actually expecting the player to roll Charisma + Persuasion or Manipulation + Etiquette). Completely normal wolves but somehow their growling translates to a human-like language. They even have names that they gave each other. Very strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an extremely long-standing conceit in WtA that the Garou have the ability to communicate fully with normal wolves (though this is not immune to negatives like high Rage). While broadly the books acknowledge this is not the same as having a conversation with humans because of the significant differences in how wolves communicate.. the books are less clear in a way to represent this effectively. A lot of groups, and a lot of fiction writers for the game itself include stuff that's in some of the gaming books not just the novels, do it like a human conversation so that it can actually be role-played on some level, and then treat it as more of a &quot;translated into spoken English so you don't have to read subtitles while actors speak a language nobody actually understands,&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> Things like &quot;do wolves have names at least internally to their packs?&quot; is also kind of a difficult question to address because it really depends on what you want to consider a name, and our inability to understand wolf vocalizations since each pack has a unique set of them. There is ample evidence that wolves do develop unique calls to identify specific individuals as a recipient of a message; it's rather understandable to do when wolves frequently hunt spread out enough to not be able to use non-vocal communication and need to coordinate who's doing what to take down prey. Is that a form of name simply because it's a unique vocal identifier to a specific individual? Depends on your definitions. Do we have any idea if those calls have deeper meanings such as referencing physical features? Not in the slightest.<br /> <br /> So you're kinda stuck if you want to have Garou interact with wolves. No option can objectively perfectly balance our best understanding of wolf communication and the needs of fictional supernatural beings that can &quot;speak wolf.&quot;<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25848\" data-vbnamecard=\"25848\">MrornX</a> there's a tag feature if you're not actually quoting us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T11:26:15-07:00","id":1559962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559959#post1559959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an extremely long-standing conceit in WtA that the Garou have the ability to communicate fully with normal wolves (though this is not immune to negatives like high Rage).</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the 'First Tongue?' Or am I remembering something from Forsaken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T12:30:43-07:00","id":1559963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559959#post1559959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's an extremely long-standing conceit in WtA that the Garou have the ability to communicate fully with normal wolves (though this is not immune to negatives like high Rage). While broadly the books acknowledge this is not the same as having a conversation with humans because of the significant differences in how wolves communicate.. the books are less clear in a way to represent this effectively. A lot of groups, and a lot of fiction writers for the game itself include stuff that's in some of the gaming books not just the novels, do it like a human conversation so that it can actually be role-played on some level, and then treat it as more of a &quot;translated into spoken English so you don't have to read subtitles while actors speak a language nobody actually understands,&quot; situation.<br /> <br /> Things like &quot;do wolves have names at least internally to their packs?&quot; is also kind of a difficult question to address because it really depends on what you want to consider a name, and our inability to understand wolf vocalizations since each pack has a unique set of them. There is ample evidence that wolves do develop unique calls to identify specific individuals as a recipient of a message; it's rather understandable to do when wolves frequently hunt spread out enough to not be able to use non-vocal communication and need to coordinate who's doing what to take down prey. Is that a form of name simply because it's a unique vocal identifier to a specific individual? Depends on your definitions. Do we have any idea if those calls have deeper meanings such as referencing physical features? Not in the slightest.<br /> <br /> So you're kinda stuck if you want to have Garou interact with wolves. No option can objectively perfectly balance our best understanding of wolf communication and the needs of fictional supernatural beings that can &quot;speak wolf.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, to me, the issue just boils down to a matter of laziness. Because this is about worldbuilding. Sure, it's easier to go for the Disney-fied approach where everyone just has to pretend that whenever Garou interact with wolves, you're in a scene from the Lion King or something and all of a sudden animals are indistinguishable from humans in how they talk. But I think any werewolf-game will lose something essential about the duality of beast and human by doing this. And while with an animistic/spiritual setting like WtA I could get behind granting animals more sapience than in the real world, I think taking the shortcut of overly humanising wolves is too much of a drawback. And there's the issue that if you're fine with overly humanising interactions with wolves, overly humanising interactions with Spirits will quickly follow afterwards. If it's easier to just humanise wolves this way, why not also apply that to Spirits as well? At that point, you might as well turn the whole thing into a Marvel-movie-esque amusement-park-ride and everybody's just delivering sardonic quips left, right and centre. <br /> <br /> And &quot;it's a difficult issue to address&quot; is what you have worldbuilding for. This werewolf-setup has created this specific issue in how something in the setting works. But when writers address this, you want to see their imagination at work, you want to see a creative answer to this issue. What you don't want is just for someone to shrug and proclaim &quot;Uhm, what if... You know how we humans do this? It's just like that.&quot;. <br /> <br /> I know it's tough to do this on the fly during a game when you're the ST but that's why it's so important for book-writers to create a framework (do worldbuilding) that will help STs deal with this issue. What doesn't help is for official releases to tell potential STs to treat wolves in their WtA-game like they're very human-like contacts that you can have discussions with and winning them over is as much a social persuasion challenge as it would be if it were a local photography-club. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T13:37:32-07:00","id":1559964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559962#post1559962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the 'First Tongue?' Or am I remembering something from Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit of both?<br /> <br /> In WtA there is a &quot;Garou Tongue&quot; (also High Tongue in some places), but that's uniquely a language that's shared by the Garou and no normal wolves are going to understand it (nor are any normal humans even if a uniquely skilled linguist and animal communication researcher could probably get some of it since it is a formal enough language that it has things like syntax and grammar).<br /> <br /> Forsaken combined Garou Tongue and the native language of spirits into First Tongue (removing the &quot;speak with spirits Gift tax&quot; and reinforcing the spiritual nature of werewolves in the game), which is labelled as the First Tongue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559963#post1559963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately, to me, the issue just boils down to a matter of laziness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? I mean, unless you have something that would widely be agreed upon as a better solution to something that's going to be used in-play disliking the current state of things isn't really going to accomplish anything. W5 putting a bit less effort than some of the older WtA books to add more flavor and color to the texts when Garou communicate with wolves (or spirits for that matter) to highlight that it works differently without making it a giant translation exercise or require a degree in wolf behavioral science to do smoothly only address one book doing a particularly lazy job of it.<br /> <br /> I'm open to the idea that there's a better way of doing it, but I've tried a bunch and they all fall flat in their own ways. The idea that it's just a failure of world-building comes off as unthinking or uncharitable. The world-building isn't that wolves actually do communicate like humans among themselves and Garou can join in, the world-building is that Garou-wolf communicate is it's own unique thing. The problem is that world-building doesn't have an easy solution to use in play.<br /> <br /> Having put some serious thought into changing things to maintain easy of play and communication in the world-building, I haven't come up with something I think is inherently better in over 20 years of trying. The only thing you can really do is narrate with as much body language as possible to emphasize things like scents and tail position modifying meaning, without forcing your players to read between the lines so you still have to translate it to human comprehensible words. Some players get into it and start to learn how to be less &quot;in translation&quot; and more focused on how you (who as the ST probably isn't doing this 100% accurately either) try to make it less human. Other players just don't care about immersion on this topic.<br /> <br /> This is very analogous to the Aura issue in other WoD games where we have these aura charts where different colors and textures have different meanings. And that's great world-building and all, but most people don't use it because you have to consult/memorize a chart just to translate what your ST is saying into what your character would know instead of your ST just telling you what your character would know. People love the world-building of seeing auras and interpreting them... but it's just an utter pain to make fun in a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But when writers address this, you want to see their imagination at work, you want to see a creative answer to this issue. </div> </div> </div>So, what do you do when this is the best and most creative answer currently available?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-14-2026, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T14:28:50-07:00","id":1559968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559964#post1559964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having put some serious thought into changing things to maintain easy of play and communication in the world-building, I haven't come up with something I think is inherently better in over 20 years of trying. The only thing you can really do is narrate with as much body language as possible to emphasize things like scents and tail position modifying meaning, without forcing your players to read between the lines so you still have to translate it to human comprehensible words. Some players get into it and start to learn how to be less &quot;in translation&quot; and more focused on how you (who as the ST probably isn't doing this 100% accurately either) try to make it less human. Other players just don't care about immersion on this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're putting in the work for the people who are into it. Of course, that won't be 100% of the people who are sitting down to play a game. And when you're writing a book, you're supposed to support the people who are into it while providing the framework that will (hopefully) convince the ones who aren't into it. Because if you're not doing that, you just end up working against yourself. <br /> <br /> It's the hurdle you have to cross with any fictional fantastical framework. But of course, there won't be any buy-in from players when the attitude is that you shouldn't even try.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, what do you do when this is the best and most creative answer currently available? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, great question. Not a loaded question at all, of course, where I can already see that no matter what I say, you will disagree with me... God, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> , why does every interaction with you have to be turned into a heated argument? <br /> <br /> Besides, you already have the answer here yourself! It's the previous quote from yourself! You acknowledged that there are people who are into it when you go for a &quot;less human&quot;-version of portraying wolves in WtA. There is an audience for this. And all I'm saying is that maybe it's better to care more about them than worrying about people who are already checked out anyway when you explain the core-tenets of the WtA-setting to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T19:23:15-07:00","id":1559974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559950#post1559950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You keep it a secret until the Times of Judgement / End Times scenario.<br /> <br /> Then you flip the script and go loud.<br /> <br /> Now, remind me, what event is currently happening within the timeframe of 5th edition?<br /> <br /> Oh, that's right. Gehenna / Apocalypse!<br /> <br /> The Antedeluvians are awake, they've put out the call to war, and the masquerade is hanging by a thread after the rise of the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> Gaia is dead, the Garou Nation has fallen, and the tribes are running around like headless chickens, with no real plan on what to do next.</div> </div> </div> </div>We already did this in the aforementioned books. WoD5 is just doing that but less good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not at all. I've got no problem with their role or duties within the game's cosmology. I simply want propagating their species to be an easier process than gacha gambling.<br /> <br /> A shame that the Skindancer ritual is accompanied by an automatic point of Wyrm Taint, or we could declare open season on the BSD's. </div> </div> </div>There are no discrete points of taint. The Ritual's text notes that unless the lives and pelts were given freely, you are heavily tainted by the Wyrm. When Sam first stepped sideways after performing the ritual, he was greeted by a shitload of banes (partially because he was already a douchebag big game hunter with a lot of trophies in a bunch of rooms that were not kept... pure, granted).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Laughs in Weaver Ascended scenario.* - You know, the one where the deific spirit responsible for humanity's progress all these millennia decides to freeze the planet in eternal stasis. </div> </div> </div>No, the Weaver isn't responsible in the way you're noting. Or even really as an indirect agent. Much like the Wyrm, it only works with what's there, and what's there was the Third Chimpanzee - less structurally sound than either chimps or bonobos, but with mechanical inclinations that even the orangutans couldn't quite match, and selection pressures for social life that eventually led to eminently brainwashable young led by elders who knew how to communicate (and being able to soak up knowledge also meant that humans could pick up the work of someone who has passed and carry it forward until it came time to pass it on).<br /> <br /> Like, I know that the 90s were an era where a lot of primatology was still figuring this out and it wasn't common knowledge among laypeople, but we have the pieces now, so there's no reason to god of the gaps human development by making them canonically altered and led by the Weaver. Humans make war against other groups of humans and record their culture for posterity on their own; the Weaver just uses it as an easy way to determine what the laws of the cosmos are so it can understand what's going on before it spins up everything into <br /> <br /> Complete! Tellurian! Stasis! [/Wesker]<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, I'm aware they're crazy enough to give the Red Talons cause for concern. But somebody ran the math on here a while ago, and determined that there should be enough Ratkin around the globe to carry out Vermintide.\u200b </div> </div> </div>There's a hard check on the r, there due to the bottleneck of the Birthing Plague. As such, the population of the Ratkin tends to hover around equal to maybe double that of the Garou. They have a much easier time filling in positions in a colony, but they're still not going to be doing Skaven numbers (which would probably just lead to their <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_W-MZt_5JHA?t=25\" target=\"_blank\">stabbing-betraying each other in the back like the Skaven</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-14T21:08:32-07:00","id":1559979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559950#post1559950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I explicitly said that it was my preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but you didn't stop there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, remind me, what event is currently happening within the timeframe of 5th edition?<br /> <br /> Oh, that's right. Gehenna / Apocalypse! </div> </div> </div>W5 is in no way a take on the Apocalypse that can justify ripping off the Veil and &quot;going loud.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to appeal to the pre-W5 ToJ scenarios transmission method doesn't matter because (1) the conceit of the setting is that all of the groups are getting rarer no matter what they try and (2) the ToJ is hitting imminently enough that we're on the last generation of the current age anyway. The Ratkin might be OK with the idea of trying to forcibly change as many humans as possible, but that doesn't actually mean it's a functional solution to any of the ToJ scenarios that would allow a future were the Fera still exist.<br /> <br /> If you want to appeal to W5, you're stuck with a whimper instead of a bang Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> If you want to try to mix them up, your point becomes incoherent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I simply want propagating their species to be an easier process than gacha gambling. </div> </div> </div>Again, a larger conceit of pre-W5 WtA is that the Garou and the Fera broadly are dying out anyway. Unless you're dumping all of the setting elements attached to that, changing transmission types doesn't fix the problem. Instead of birth rates dropping, you'd have less bites ending in a new Garou and more ending in dead humans that before to keep the same mood of the game.<br /> <br /> And of course, you can't propagate a specifies by spreading a curse/infection. If werewolves are just humans with a magical disease, spreading the disease isn't propagating werewolves as a species, it's just purposefully spreading a disease around so more humans have it. If you want a separate species that propagates, the &quot;gacha&quot; of birth is the only way that actually happens; though I find that comparison nonsensical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A shame that the Skindancer ritual is accompanied by an automatic point of Wyrm Taint, or we could declare open season on the BSD's. </div> </div> </div>I'll actually address something <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> said here as in some editions Taint did have point ratings and the ritual was written with that in mind.<br /> <br /> Of course, this still goes against your idea of wanting easier spread of Fera... kill five for one human to take their place? That math doesn't math. Yeah, I get it, you hunt the bad ones.. but plenty of humans and Kinfolk don't think that the Gaia loyal groups are good guys either and if you spread the ritual around, you don't control who gets it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Laughs in Weaver Ascended scenario.* - You know, the one where the deific spirit responsible for humanity's progress all these millennia decides to freeze the planet in eternal stasis. </div> </div> </div>And this has nothing to do with what I said so... whatever. I got beaten to addressing this more specifically, and I stand by how evolution actually works instead of some C- grade high school biology understanding of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, I'm aware they're crazy enough to give the Red Talons cause for concern. But somebody ran the math on here a while ago, and determined that there should be enough Ratkin around the globe to carry out Vermintide.\u200b </div> </div> </div>O...K...<br /> <br /> Did you miss the whole point about the issue being the Ratkin's difficulty in agreement and coordination more than their ability to cause a massive global plague?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559968#post1559968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you're putting in the work for the people who are into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I put in the work for my friends to make the game fun for them. I'm not a professional TTRPG writer or developer (or even something less than professional as I've never published anything in a complete and final form even for free use).<br /> <br /> As for the actual game designers, yes I agree with you on what the ideal is. My point is what the reality is where you can't always get to the ideal.<br /> <br /> And there's a side point of this particular issue not necessarily being as important to a lot of people as you're expressing it is to you. Most groups I've played WtA with don't feel super strongly either way as long as either extreme is avoided: wolf communication needs to be given some acknowledgement, but nobody wants to distract from playing the game to make sure they're describing the correct angle and directionality of tail wagging instead of just being able to say, &quot;my PC's tail is in an alert and cautious position.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But of course, there won't be any buy-in from players when the attitude is that you shouldn't even try. </div> </div> </div>Outside of one W5 book... what's your evidence that most of the WtA authors are of this opinion? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not a loaded question at all, of course, where I can already see that no matter what I say, you will disagree with me... God, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> , why does every interaction with you have to be turned into a heated argument? </div> </div> </div>This fucking baffles me.<br /> <br /> While I could appreciate some sort of objection to it being a leading question... so what? I asked it to make a rhetorical point. If you want to address the point without directly answering the question, whatever.<br /> <br /> Then you dig into me personally and want to make it my fault that things heat up? Seriously, what the hell? Nothing was heated until this. You decided you knew how I was going to respond to your response so you preemptively make snide comments at me and that's my fault? Yeah. No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, you already have the answer here yourself! It's the previous quote from yourself! You acknowledged that there are people who are into it when you go for a &quot;less human&quot;-version of portraying wolves in WtA. There is an audience for this. And all I'm saying is that maybe it's better to care more about them than worrying about people who are already checked out anyway when you explain the core-tenets of the WtA-setting to them. </div> </div> </div>My previous post was pretty clear that I've tried multiple approaches to Garou-wolf communication over the years in my personal games and not had more success than &quot;doing it as if everyone's speaking human and acknowledging that in reality they're doing it as wolves,&quot; in the total pay out in play.<br /> <br /> The solution of &quot;just focus on one type of player,&quot; doesn't work if I don't have a lot of players and this isn't a serious sticking point for any of them. High immersion wolf communication RP is not a core-tenet of WtA play for... anyone I've ever played with. It's a pretty niche part of the game and I'm not turning great players away for not caring much about it when there's so much else in the game everyone in the group actually does care about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T20:41:14-07:00","id":1560001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559974#post1559974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the Weaver isn't responsible in the way you're noting. Or even really as an indirect agent. Much like the Wyrm, it only works with what's there, and what's there was the Third Chimpanzee - less structurally sound than either chimps or bonobos, but with mechanical inclinations that even the orangutans couldn't quite match, and selection pressures for social life that eventually led to eminently brainwashable young led by elders who knew how to communicate (and being able to soak up knowledge also meant that humans could pick up the work of someone who has passed and carry it forward until it came time to pass it on).<br /> <br /> Like, I know that the 90s were an era where a lot of primatology was still figuring this out and it wasn't common knowledge among laypeople, but we have the pieces now, so there's no reason to god of the gaps human development by making them canonically altered and led by the Weaver. Humans make war against other groups of humans and record their culture for posterity on their own; the Weaver just uses it as an easy way to determine what the laws of the cosmos are so it can understand what's going on before it spins up everything into</div> </div> </div> </div>So then, what exactly is Weaver doing in this setting? Because I thought the Triumvirate was<br /> <br /> Wyld - makes it.<br /> <br /> Weaver - gives it purpose.<br /> <br /> Wyrm - recycles it when that purpose has been served.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> Without the Weaver, humanity would have no purpose. It would just be another one of the Wyld's hastily made gorgons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T20:54:58-07:00","id":1560002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559974#post1559974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We already did this in the aforementioned books. WoD5 is just doing that but less good.</div> </div> </div> </div>They should have made 5th edition take place after the Times of Judgement, instead of during it. I think a setting where you try to pick up the pieces of a broken world and rebuild would have made for a very compelling narrative. Especially for a series titled <i>&quot;World of Darkness&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559974#post1559974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's a hard check on the r, there due to the bottleneck of the Birthing Plague. As such, the population of the Ratkin tends to hover around equal to maybe double that of the Garou. They have a much easier time filling in positions in a colony, but they're still not going to be doing Skaven numbers (which would probably just lead to their <a href=\"https://youtu.be/_W-MZt_5JHA?t=25\" target=\"_blank\">stabbing-betraying each other in the back like the Skaven</a>).</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need ALL the Ratkin to be on board with the plan. Just enough of them to feasibly get the job done.<br /> <br /> Also, even if we go by Krogan standards and say that only 1 rat out of every 1,000 undergoes the First Change, the writers still underestimate how quickly rats breed.<br /> <br /> Tacking on the fact that mundane rats only live between 2 to 4 years, the Ratkin would have to fuck like Kobolds, if they wanted to maintain their colonies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T21:11:22-07:00","id":1560003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559979#post1559979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but you didn't stop there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> W5 is in no way a take on the Apocalypse that can justify ripping off the Veil and &quot;going loud.&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gaia is dead, the gauntlet is much, much harder to pass through, the Garou nation has fallen, we've lost our greatest warriors to some human ideology, and now the government has gotten its shit together and is launching a full organized manhunt against the supernatural community.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but what part of this sequence of worst case scenarios tells you <i>&quot;oh yes, we need to exercise restraint?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559979#post1559979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, a larger conceit of pre-W5 WtA is that the Garou and the Fera broadly are dying out anyway. Unless you're dumping all of the setting elements attached to that, changing transmission types doesn't fix the problem. Instead of birth rates dropping, you'd have less bites ending in a new Garou and more ending in dead humans that before to keep the same mood of the game.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Survival of the fittest, that's how nature works. You make the mistake of thinking my goal is to save humanity. It's not; within the context of the W:tA setting, I wholly endorse the Impergium, because I agree with the Red Talon sentiment. The idea of humanity serving as agents of the apocalypse is not black pilled doomer speak within this setting. It is an objective fact, backed up by empirical evidence for those who study the metaplot.<br /> <br /> Getting rid of Humanity may not solve the issue, but it would dramatically set the Wyrm back in its progress.<br /> <br /> But since we've reached a point where global genocide is no longer a feasible option, then mass conversion will have to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1559979#post1559979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And of course, you can't propagate a specifies by spreading a curse/infection. If werewolves are just humans with a magical disease, spreading the disease isn't propagating werewolves as a species, it's just purposefully spreading a disease around so more humans have it. If you want a separate species that propagates, the &quot;gacha&quot; of birth is the only way that actually happens; though I find that comparison nonsensical.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, a propagating species would be something that actually breeds true, passing on its genetics from parent to child. Not something that just randomly strikes out of nowhere,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T21:33:15-07:00","id":1560007,"title":"","content":"First, it's important to remember that the Triat are vast cosmic entities that are highly detached from the reality of human-scale thinking and thus don't really go around trying to explain things (unlike Gaia and the Celestines who might be vast but have maintained more personal connections to smaller entities). <br /> <br /> From that, the books have repeatedly made it clear that nobody really knows anything other than exceptional broad and practically tautological aspects of them. There are multiple interpretations and so on among the various creatures of the WoD and even in WtA there is plenty of disagreement between a number of groups on how the Triat is both supposed to work, and how it's actually working now.<br /> <br /> From the traditionalist Gaian aligned perspective, the biggest issue with your statements on this is the use of the word &quot;purpose.&quot; The Triat don't deal in things like &quot;purpose.&quot; They are forces that do according to their nature. Gaia is the origin of purpose in the cosmology named after her; since that cosmology assumes that the universal aspect of Gaia is above the Triat instead of others that put her as equal or even below them in the hierarchy of things. In this cosmology (which most WtA characters are going to default to) the Wyld creates chaotically, the Weaver takes that and gives it structure and stability so it can operate after the Wyld moves on to its next creation, and the Wyrm destroys to avoid the universe getting clogged up with the output of the other two.<br /> <br /> The second most common take is that the pre-fall Balance Wyrm was a moderating force between the chaos of the Wyld and the order of the Weaver and it destroyed what was necessary to keep the universe in a healthy cycle. The distinct is slight but the Destroyer Wyrm is indiscriminate that cares more about a &quot;quota&quot; of elimination, where the Balance Wyrm is more intentional in destroying specific things based on the cosmic impact achieved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T22:07:19-07:00","id":1560008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560007#post1560007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the traditionalist Gaian aligned perspective, the biggest issue with your statements on this is the use of the word &quot;purpose.&quot; The Triat don't deal in things like &quot;purpose.&quot; They are forces that do according to their nature. Gaia is the origin of purpose in the cosmology named after her; since that cosmology assumes that the universal aspect of Gaia is above the Triat instead of others that put her as equal or even below them in the hierarchy of things. In this cosmology (which most WtA characters are going to default to) the Wyld creates chaotically, the Weaver takes that and gives it structure and stability so it can operate after the Wyld moves on to its next creation, and the Wyrm destroys to avoid the universe getting clogged up with the output of the other two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that just sounds like Gaian propaganda. The Wyld is the spirit of creation. She couldn't have created anything before the very concept of creation itself existed. And if she were above them in the spiritual hierarchy, then logically speaking, she should have been able to give the Triat a good smack upside the head when they attempted to destroy her.<br /> <br /> The last time one of the Triat got pissed off at Luna, they proceeded to eradicate all life on every moon in the universe. Gaia, who as far as we can tell, is supposed to be the spirit of the universe, did nothing to stop them, and has continued to do nothing to reverse the damage it caused.<br /> <br /> The feud between Wyld and Wyrm has also raged on for countless eons. With countless universes being created, destroyed, and recreated in an endless cycle. So in the grand scheme of things, Gaia being destroyed is not a major issue. She is replaceable, while the Triat (in theory) are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T22:15:44-07:00","id":1560009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GreatHornedRatkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560003#post1560003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia is dead, the gauntlet is much, much harder to pass through, the Garou nation has fallen, we've lost our greatest warriors to some human ideology, and now the government has gotten its shit together and is launching a full organized manhunt against the supernatural community.<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but what part of this sequence of worst case scenarios tells you <i>&quot;oh yes, we need to exercise restraint?&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about restraint. It's about the practical reality on the ground for the Garou of W5. Without the Garou Nation (and OOC with the massive nerf they took via their mental health tracks), they have no way to organize mass scale revolutions against humanity; esp. a newly empowered technological and aware-of-the-supernatural government lead humanity.<br /> <br /> As I said, W5 is a whimper of an apocalypse. The time and ability to make the kind of difference you're talking about has passed already. As it stands in W5, a movement to &quot;go loud&quot; is just going to get shut down by silver bullet armed spec ops soldiers before it can do anything that can't be covered up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Survival of the fittest, that's how nature works. </div> </div> </div>Survival of the fittest is how one specific aspect of nature works. And most people do not appreciate the highly specific definition of the phrase used in biology.<br /> <br /> This is the whole problem with &quot;humans have lost touch with nature!&quot; nonsense if you want to apply actual evolution. Survival of the fittest is nature. Humans have developed one of the most potent survival skill sets in evolutionary history and that makes us exceptionally fit (though it's possible we're a burn bright and fast species since we haven't been around that long). Our massive cities are as much nature as termite mounds and beaver dams. Our weapons as are much nature as claws and fangs. We optimized for fitness by technology and the only thing that is any real threat to us in fitness terms at this point is ourselves. Species with evolutionary fitness that worked for hundreds of millions of years are getting trashed by us. The fitness &quot;meta&quot; has shifted, as it has many times in the past and will do again.<br /> <br /> Humanity is not somehow &quot;doing nature wrong.&quot; We're doing exactly what nature demands of us. That's why there's so damned many of us; because we keep toppling everything in nature that would reduce our fitness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You make the mistake of thinking my goal is to save humanity. </div> </div> </div>You keep saying that I'm making mistakes by not being a mind reader as I can't know what points you're secretly making when I respond to what you're asking posting. It's getting annoying and pathetic. If you're not communicating your points well, than you need to do better. And whether or not you care about the fate of humanity is irrelevant to any point I made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...within the context of the W:tA setting, I wholly endorse the Impergium, because I agree with the Red Talon sentiment. The idea of humanity serving as agents of the apocalypse is not black pilled doomer speak within this setting. It is an objective fact, backed up by empirical evidence for those who study the metaplot. </div> </div> </div>The Impergium didn't work, as the metaplot made abundantly clear. Even when it was in full effect, humans were expanding in number and technology fueled fitness.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons are idiots that don't understand anything about population control, evolution, and nature. Their philosophy is a thinly veiled pretense to justify violence born of the anger of sore losers. Survival of the fittest? Humans proved more fit than wolves. Nature doesn't care about saving the loser of this situation. If you want to maximize your survival fitness, you don't decide the massive human intellect you have running alongside your wolf body is evil and thus reject using it to its full potential.<br /> <br /> The idea that humanity as a whole serves anything in the setting other than itself is 100% black pilled doomer bullshit.<br /> <br /> Failure to retract your blatant lie that this is somehow &quot;objectively&quot; true based on the metaplot is a clear admission on your behalf that you're trolling motivated by a complete hatred of WtA and only post in WtA spaces to poison the well and drive people away from the game. It's kinda hard to not see through this when you massively swung from &quot;Humanity served the Weaver&quot; to &quot;Humanity serves the Wyrm&quot; as soon as you needed to make a different rhetorical point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But since we've reached a point where global genocide is no longer a feasible option, then mass conversion will have to do. </div> </div> </div>It's laughable that you think studying the metaplot would ever lead to the idea that global genocide is a solution to anything. Genocide empowers the Wyrm. Genocide would be a great case for humanity &quot;serving&quot; the Wyrm, but then you couldn't define genociding humans with the Red Talons anti-nature zealots.<br /> <br /> And of course, you overlook an actual interesting conversation on if the Ratkin can pull off a mass plague even if they are hypothetically capable of it if everything lines up right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, a propagating species would be something that actually breeds true, passing on its genetics from parent to child. Not something that just randomly strikes out of nowhere, </div> </div> </div>How am I supposed to read this as anything other than trolling?<br /> <br /> Breed true? Breed true means reproducing sexually! If you want breeding true from parent to child, you want werewolf transmission as it works in the game. Transmission like a disease is what just randomly strikes out of nowhere.<br /> <br /> I get I made some typos here and there that could be read uncharitably as a bit hypocritical, but this is beyond the pale of that. You're claiming the exact opposite of what you want is somehow what you want through the magic back box of whatever you think evolution and reproduction are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-15T22:40:38-07:00","id":1560011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560008#post1560008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that just sounds like Gaian propaganda.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK... and any other explanation is going to sound like the propaganda of the group you're listening to. That's sort of the nature of metaphysical cosmology discussions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wyld is the spirit of creation. </div> </div> </div>There are lots of spirits of creation in the books, and few of them are aligned with the Wyld. Most of the Wyld aligned entities in the books are far more associated with chaos rather than purposeful creation. The Flux Realm itself is just utter chaos that spits out infinitely unique results with no discernible rhyme or reason.<br /> <br /> If Gaia is the origin of purpose, nothing can exist before her because she gives everything its purpose; even the Wyld. And this isn't a logical issue as the Wyld doesn't seem to create with purpose as I already noted. WtA cosmology does not call for unique domains where only one spirit can be the spirit of something and thus everything subject to having that quality most come from one and only one spirit. Gaia and the Wyld can both be creative forces in their own ways without being a contradiction in the established metaphysics of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if she were above them in the spiritual hierarchy, then logically speaking, she should have been able to give the Triat a good smack upside the head when they attempted to destroy her. </div> </div> </div>It's an animist cosmology. Even the universal Gaia isn't omnipotent like the way real world monotheists describe their deity of choice. It has long been hinted at in the books that it is a distinct possibility that between creating the Triat and creating various things on Earth, Gaia was too diminished to oppose the Triat if they got up to something as a group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The last time one of the Triat got pissed off at Luna, they proceeded to eradicate all life on every moon in the universe. </div> </div> </div>What... exactly are you talking about? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The feud between Wyld and Wyrm has also raged on for countless eons. </div> </div> </div>We have no idea on exactly when the Triat became imbalanced and thus when the normal order of their original operations turned into active hostilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With countless universes being created, destroyed, and recreated in an endless cycle. </div> </div> </div>This is not present in the WtA setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So in the grand scheme of things, Gaia being destroyed is not a major issue. She is replaceable, while the Triat (in theory) are not. </div> </div> </div>If you decide to take a Triat-primary cosmology? Potentially. But as the vast majority of takes in the books despite the relation of Gaia to the Triat still treat the Triat more as cosmic forces dedicated only to fulfilling their spiritual nature to the maximum extent they can with minimal if any true agency, powerful spiritual entities with sufficient agencies would still be necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T00:40:01-07:00","id":1560013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560011#post1560011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK... and any other explanation is going to sound like the propaganda of the group you're listening to. That's sort of the nature of metaphysical cosmology discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that is not even remotely accurate.<br /> <br /> I reject the Gaian propaganda, because it's trying to say that Gaia created the very concept of creation, instead of the other way around. Which is a logical paradox, similar to time travel.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560011#post1560011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There are lots of spirits of creation in the books, and few of them are aligned with the Wyld. Most of the Wyld aligned entities in the books are far more associated with chaos rather than purposeful creation. The Flux Realm itself is just utter chaos that spits out infinitely unique results with no discernible rhyme or reason.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Wyld is the Big C. He is the deific personification of creation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560011#post1560011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If Gaia is the origin of purpose, nothing can exist before her because she gives everything its purpose; even the Wyld. And this isn't a logical issue as the Wyld doesn't seem to create with purpose as I already noted. WtA cosmology does not call for unique domains where only one spirit can be the spirit of something and thus everything subject to having that quality most come from one and only one spirit. Gaia and the Wyld can both be creative forces in their own ways without being a contradiction in the established metaphysics of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said anything about Wyld being the one to give things purpose. All I said was that he is the spirit of creation. As in the act of performing it, not the existence thereof.<br /> <br /> Weaver is the one who gives things purpose and meaning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560011#post1560011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's an animist cosmology. Even the universal Gaia isn't omnipotent like the way real world monotheists describe their deity of choice. It has long been hinted at in the books that it is a distinct possibility that between creating the Triat and creating various things on Earth, Gaia was too diminished to oppose the Triat if they got up to something as a group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which they have not done for millions of years, ever since Weaver went crazy and disrupted the balance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560011#post1560011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What... exactly are you talking about?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The moons used to have life on them. They were flourishing, life sustaining planetoids in their own right. But then Luna went and pissed off one of the Triat, (I think it might have been Weaver?) and they retaliated by destroying all life on Luna. And since Luna is the spiritual concept of the moon, this resulted in every moon becoming a desolate wasteland.<br /> <br /> Now, Luna's only roommate is Coyote. Who crashed on her couch one day and refuses to leave.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560011#post1560011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you decide to take a Triat-primary cosmology? Potentially. But as the vast majority of takes in the books despite the relation of Gaia to the Triat still treat the Triat more as cosmic forces dedicated only to fulfilling their spiritual nature to the maximum extent they can with minimal if any true agency, powerful spiritual entities with sufficient agencies would still be necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I hate the unreliable narrator metaplot so much. It makes it damn near impossible to have a serious debate with anybody on these forums, because no matter what one of us says, the other can always retort with a <i>&quot;well actually&quot; </i>response.<br /> <br /> There needs to be at least SOME sense of established canon, or else any discussions involving the lore become a pointless waste of time and energy.\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T01:14:54-07:00","id":1560014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560013#post1560013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that is not even remotely accurate.<br /> <br /> I reject the Gaian propaganda, because it's trying to say that Gaia created the very concept of creation, instead of the other way around. Which is a logical paradox, similar to time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, perhaps like in some cosmological setups, Gaia didn't have to be born, and she just existed. You might not find it likely, but it's not like it's less likely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but Wyld is the Big C. He is the deific personification of creation. </div> </div> </div>They could be. But, again, no guaranteeing that he created everything if something already existed. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said anything about Wyld being the one to give things purpose. All I said was that he is the spirit of creation. As in the act of performing it, not the existence thereof.<br /> <br /> Weaver is the one who gives things purpose and meaning. </div> </div> </div>Ideally, and when the text is consistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which they have not done for millions of years, ever since Weaver went crazy and disrupted the balance. </div> </div> </div>Technically, the maddened Wyrm and the Weaver are acting in concert to beat the shit out of the Wyld. Gaia's actions (by proxy, of course) could be seen as an attempt to save the Wyld, even though the Wyld is still a seething alien pot of madness in their own right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The moons used to have life on them. They were flourishing, life sustaining planetoids in their own right. But then Luna went and pissed off one of the Triat, (I think it might have been Weaver?) and they retaliated by destroying all life on Luna. And since Luna is the spiritual concept of the moon, this resulted in every moon becoming a desolate wasteland. </div> </div> </div>According to the Ananasi. They would, of course, never lie, cannot be subverted by the Triat that they pretend to work for, and are perfectly trustworthy.<br /> <br /> /s <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, Luna's only roommate is Coyote. Who crashed on her couch one day and refuses to leave. </div> </div> </div>Surely the Bastet Jamaak as well. And the various Moon Incarnae under her. And Chimera, since the Stargazers are closest to Sokhta in RatH. And the list could honestly keep going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why I hate the unreliable narrator metaplot so much. It makes it damn near impossible to have a serious debate with anybody on these forums, because no matter what one of us says, the other can always retort with a <i>&quot;well actually&quot; </i>response.<br /> <br /> There needs to be at least SOME sense of established canon, or else any discussions involving the lore become a pointless waste of time and energy.\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>Generally, the established canon in W:tA IS that Gaia is the top spirit because the books do tend to get written with that point of view in mind. Even dissenting Fera opinions on that got changed by Revised, since Revised was trying to get everyone on the same page to unite and band together against the the Triatic Wyrms driving around the Wyrm's &quot;Body&quot; for a lack of a better term and the maddened Weaver.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T02:02:43-07:00","id":1560016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560013#post1560013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, that is not even remotely accurate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it is. You can't have objective discussions of what comes down to mystic belief structures. There's no out-of-character objective detailed definition of these entities. They're supposed to be vast and incomprehensible, something not served well if the authors nail down many details that makes most in-universe interpretations of them incorrect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I reject the Gaian propaganda, because it's trying to say that Gaia created the very concept of creation, instead of the other way around. </div> </div> </div>What is and what isn't &quot;Gaian propaganda&quot; that's backed up by actual material from the books?<br /> <br /> Gaia is frequently cited as the creative spirit of the universe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is a logical paradox, similar to time travel. </div> </div> </div>We're talking mythologies and metaphysics. Formal logic rules do not apply. Lots of deities in real world myths do things that are strictly logical paradoxes that they can do because they're that powerful; they are gods after all. The very notion that any form of deity or spirit created the universe is a logical paradox because it can't have created itself or created whatever created it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but Wyld is the Big C. He is the deific personification of creation. </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting this?<br /> <br /> I'm going to quote things because it seems we're at that point. From W20:<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Weaver, The:</b> Manifestation and symbol of order and pattern. Computers, science, logic, and mathematics are examples of the Weaver\u2019s influence on the material plane.<br /> <b>Wyld, The:</b> Manifestation and symbol of pure change; the chaos of transmutation and elemental force.<br /> <b>Wyrm, The:</b> Manifestation and symbol of evil, entropy, and decay in Garou belief. Vampires are often considered manifestations of the Wyrm, as are toxic waste and pollution.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's from the lexicon. Note that &quot;creation&quot; isn't even present.<br /> <br /> &quot;Creation begins with the Wyld, the prime agent of change in the cosmos. In fact, the Wyld is more than chaos: it\u2019s a perpetual process of transmutation. The Wyld drives evolution and adaptation, as endless variations of the creative process result in the advancement of living things. The Wyld is possibility and random chance incarnate, responsible for everything from hopes and dreams to the fear that everything we possess will be lost by sudden catastrophe. It\u2019s equally liberating and terrifying.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> And that's from chapter 7 under the Wyld subhead of the Triat section. It never says that the Wyld <b>is</b> creation, or the Big C as you put it. It says that creation beings with the Wyld. The words used to define what the Wyld is are expand on the basic lexicon definition without getting to your asserted position. I will note this section is not stated to be from the Gaian perspective and is written in an out-of-character voice. Though later in the section it does say something about what some Garou believe:<br /> <br /> &quot;Some Garou blindly insist that Gaia Herself came from the Wyld, for she could never exist without it. Nothing could.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> So... still rejecting Gaian propaganda? Or not when some of it agrees with your stance?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said anything about Wyld being the one to give things purpose. </div> </div> </div>I didn't say you did. I said Gaia is the one that gives things purpose according to the majority views presented in the texts, and that includes giving the Wyld it's purpose as the Triat member of creativity and change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Weaver is the one who gives things purpose and meaning. </div> </div> </div>Again, where are you getting this?<br /> <br /> So scrolling down from above:<br /> <br /> &quot;The unlimited ambitions of the Wyld must eventually gave way to ordered growth. With a few strands, the Weaver anchored the turbulent vortex of the Wyld\u2019s creation, naturally selecting the most promising creations to endure, thereby saving them from falling back into the maelstrom of the Wyld\u2019s endless creation. Limitless chaos was structured and given form. From these simple lines and strands, patterns took shape, as the Weaver began constructing the fundamental structure of the universe: the Pattern Web. Wherever there was form, there could be growth and progress. Inconstant infinity yielded to enduring eternity.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> Again, consistent with the lexicon, and no mention of purpose and meaning. The Weaver takes from the Wyld's chaos and builds form and function, stability and structure; making order of the chaos. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which they have not done for millions of years, ever since Weaver went crazy and disrupted the balance. </div> </div> </div>Again, there is no established time frame in the books for when this happened. Do you have a citation for &quot;millions of years.&quot; Because I can quote things that imply more like ten or twenty thousand as the imbalance finally reached the tipping point as humanity moved towards the earliest steps of organized agriculture and civilization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The moons used to have life on them. </div> </div> </div>What books are you getting this from? I can't find any that even talk about what's going on with the moons of the solar system, let alone extrasolar moons. The Moon, abode of Luna, is the only moon with anything more than possibly getting named in the texts I've checked, and it has life on it (if mostly in the form of mages). I can find nothing saying that all of the moons of the universe used to have life on them until a Triat member got pissed at Luna. Hell, I can't find a reference to one of them getting specifically upset at her. The books repeatedly talk about how disconnected the Triat are from the Celestines and Incarnae, they don't care what Luna, Helios, and so on do on a personal level. You can assert this as many times as you want, but you're going to have to start putting up some text to back yourself up to make it mean anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And since Luna is the spiritual concept of the moon, this resulted in every moon becoming a desolate wasteland. </div> </div> </div>So... why does Luna have a personal garden on the moon where her Incarnae can host Garou vistors without them going insane from their Rage going out of control if they touch the material or spiritual surface of the moon? Because that's explicitly something that exists as per Rage Across the Heavens; a book that also puts the other moons as parts of the domains of their respective planetary spirits. Phobos and Deimos are part of Nerigal's domain, not Luna's... so the idea that they're lifeless because of her makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, Luna's only roommate is Coyote. Who crashed on her couch one day and refuses to leave. </div> </div> </div>Seriously... are you just taking the piss here? Sokhta, Phoebe (maybe the same spirit, maybe two different faces of the same spirit), and Moira are all Incarnae of Luna that explicitly live on the Moon full time along with a host of Lune spirits. The Technocracy and the Sons of Ether both have bases on the moon (or had depending on where in various time-lines you want to be given M20's Future Fates options). There's also a mysterious other faction that's attacking the VE's on the moon so you can run Aliens style Space Marines vs. Xenomorph fights there; even before the potential danger of Threat Null attacking the base.<br /> <br /> Whoever told you it's just Luna and Coyote is giving you bad info. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is why I hate the unreliable narrator metaplot so much. It makes it damn near impossible to have a serious debate with anybody on these forums, because no matter what one of us says, the other can always retort with a <i>&quot;well actually&quot; </i>response. </div> </div> </div>I can't change how the books are written, but the biggest detractor from having a fruitful conversation about this seems to be you refusing to actually check what's even written. You're throwing things away as &quot;Gaian propaganda&quot; and just asserting things as if they're commonly known facts; even though you have multiple times in the past admitted to getting your information on the game second hand.<br /> <br /> I haven't &quot;well actually&quot; here. I've been as clear as I can be about presenting what the books cite as the traditional cosmology of the WtA setting. I've even presented alternate takes. You're the one just going, &quot;well this has to be true because of a fact I can't even point to being from a book in the game logically would kinda mean maybe it should be true.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There needs to be at least SOME sense of established canon, or else any discussions involving the lore become a pointless waste of time and energy.\u200b\u200b\u200b </div> </div> </div>1) Canon has nothing to do with what kind of narrator the authors use to voice a text, nor if the text is functionally coherent enough for deep lore discussions. Canon just means some body of people recognized as authoritative have said &quot;these works count, and these ones don't,&quot; or possibly some tier of levels of canon (Lucas had a multi-tier canon for Star Wars before he sold it to Disney that got... complicated). There is a sense of established canon here: what the actually gaming books say. OG White Wolf, WW under CCP, WW under Paradox, and Paradox by itself, have consistently used a simple metric: gaming books are the canon unless noted specifically (happened to a W20 book), secondary media are either non-canon or should be disregarded if they contradict the gaming books. So we just go with what's in the gaming books because those are the official canon. This doesn't resolve everything (multiple editions, crossover discussions), but for an internal WtA cosmology discussion? We have a canon to fall back on.<br /> <br /> 2) If the authors decide certain aspects of the setting are to be undefined in canon, that's just what it is. We can have a discussion about it, but it means tempering our statements with the knowledge that unreliable narrator is in effect because the authors didn't want one answer to be the canon truth. TTRPGs do this a lot because they want us to be able to have mysteries in the game that don't have one answer so we can revisit them with new eyes and new takes on them. But if you want to avoid wasting time you have to actually use the canon material that points to potential answers to these questions even if they're not explicitly The Answer. When you just dismiss a whole bunch of stuff because &quot;that's just Gaian propaganda!&quot; you're making the discussion harder to have a point; not less. If you want alternate takes on things, they're in the books, but as I noted, you're just picking who's unreliable story you want to put forward as the starting point, not picking something that isn't subject to in-universe bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T02:26:59-07:00","id":1560018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560014#post1560014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, perhaps like in some cosmological setups, Gaia didn't have to be born, and she just existed. You might not find it likely, but it's not like it's less likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm actually debating a second hand take on Ananasa's version of the formation of the WtA universe... she explicitly says the Wyrm was first and was just there because before something there was nothing and the Wyrm is the spirit of nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> According to the Ananasi. They would, of course, never lie, cannot be subverted by the Triat that they pretend to work for, and are perfectly trustworthy. </div> </div> </div>I actually broke out the Ananasi book when you pointed this out... And it's not just according to some random narrator spider, the chapter starts with the narrator being Ananasa herself... and she even starts with, &quot;I believe...&quot; since she starts by narrating a bunch of stuff that happened before she existed. And her story is biased as hell to make her on par with Gaia and the Triat (though she puts the Triat above Gaia), and despite claiming that the Weaver gives things purpose... for some reason she has to constantly remind the Weaver that things aren't going to plan because the Weaver can't seem to remember what those purposes were. Her story includes the moon (and just the moon, not all moons) because the Weaver tried to make perfect life there to show up the life the Wyld made on Earth... only for it to fail instantly because it was pure stasis and broke apart when trying to carry out the functions of life. Luna doesn't really seem to care nor did she do anything to cause the situation.<br /> <br /> The whole section is basically just Ananasa talking herself up and how Spider was the ultimate creation made possible by her drawing from all of the Triat and Gaia since none of them could act in a fashion outside of their spiritual nature while she could (despite the story including the Triat all acting outside of their nature at least once...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T02:47:15-07:00","id":1560019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560016#post1560016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is and what isn't &quot;Gaian propaganda&quot; that's backed up by actual material from the books?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Backed up by who? Because once again: unreliable narrator.<br /> <br /> You've got dozens of different takes about how, when and why stuff happened, and they're all shouting over each other, saying they're the right answer.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, the Rokea. They claim that their creator once possessed a magical pearl that contained the very spirit of Humanity itself within it, and that whoever possessed this pearl would thus be able to control humanity on a spiritual level.<br /> <br /> Only for the Ananasi to claim that this so called 'pearl' was actually the amber prison which Queen Ananasa has been trapped inside, and is currently in the possession of the Wyrm, after they stole it from Weaver.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560016#post1560016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaia is frequently cited as the creative spirit of the universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>So has the biblical God of Abrahamic faiths, which is presented in both Vampire and Demon.<br /> <br /> Remember that in World of Darkness, all the various splats and their mythos exist within the same universal cosmology. Thus turning the metaplot into a gargantuan, convoluted mess.<br /> <br /> At least Chronicles had the forethought of making each splat take place within their own self contained narrative.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560016#post1560016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again, where are you getting this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh, from actually knowing anything about the Weaver? Hell, you just defended my point for me, when you quoted from the lexicon.<br /> <br /> They are the spirit of order and patterns. They take chaos, and give it a sense of direction and meaning.<br /> <br /> It's the Wyld's job to give you a set of gills and 3 extra pairs of arms, but it's Weaver's job to figure out what you're supposed to do with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560016#post1560016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Again, there is no established time frame in the books for when this happened. Do you have a citation for &quot;millions of years.&quot; Because I can quote things that imply more like ten or twenty thousand as the imbalance finally reached the tipping point as humanity moved towards the earliest steps of organized agriculture and civilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>My citations are the Makole and Rokea, both of whom have been roaming the earth since the time of the dinosaurs. Humanity was nowhere to be found in those ancient periods.<br /> <br /> <br /> Until the day they finally did emerge, and the Makole took on the role of Dragon Kings, helping to uplift the hairless apes from their primitive existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T03:17:42-07:00","id":1560021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560019#post1560019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Backed up by who? Because once again: unreliable narrator.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be missing my point on this:<br /> <br /> If you want an actual discussion on this, you need to stop taking sides and treating anything as the &quot;right&quot; group to cite. Even the Mokole or Rokea.<br /> <br /> That's what having a discussion about something presented with an unreliable narrator entails. If you just go around saying, &quot;Well screw this group, I'm going with that group,&quot; it's not a discussion that going anyway. If you want to make a case for why we should treat a group as the group to default to, make a case from the books. Is your group's biased consistently in line with the non-biased statements from the authors? Is there a vital coherence in the setting that only that group addresses? Give a reason with stuff from the books on why an answer if picking one answer is even worth it.<br /> <br /> These discussions require more work on all of our parts to build points up than just &quot;passage X in book Y clearly says Z.&quot; like you can with simpler topics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember that in World of Darkness, all the various splats and their mythos exist within the same universal cosmology. Thus turning the metaplot into a gargantuan, convoluted mess. </div> </div> </div>You seem to have missed my pointing to this.<br /> <br /> But that's also irrelevant. We don't need to go outside of WtA for what we're talking about. And having a whole discussion on how to treat the WoD's mixed cosmology is an entire other thing that doesn't feel fruitful to get into here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least Chronicles had the forethought of making each splat take place within their own self contained narrative. </div> </div> </div>What?<br /> <br /> The CofD is a single unified setting. The CofD works because it learned from the mistakes of the original WoD run and makes sure each splat as enough room to do its own thing or crossover without setting conceit issues (other issues still happen). The WoD is a mess because it started with the idea that each group was its own self-contained narrative and vampires dealt with &quot;Lupines&quot; who may or may not be the Garou. But as crossover got more popular with the fans (which also happened fast), they moved to unify the WoD as one overarching universe post hoc and that's when it got messy. And Revised tried to fix things with the bubbles-on-a-pool-cosmology but that never really caught on because only a few authors were really pushing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uhh, from actually knowing anything about the Weaver? Hell, you just defended my point for me, when you quoted from the lexicon. </div> </div> </div>You seem to be missing the point of quoting the books because the quotes from the books do not support your take on the Weaver. You're adding in words no present to twist the text into being more supportive of what you're saying. That's why I also quoted the larger sections. The Weaver is not the spirit of giving things direction and meaning; so interpretations add that on, but it's not the constant definition like giving form and structure are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My citations are the Makole and Rokea,.. </div> </div> </div>That's an appeal, not a citation. An appeal is when you point to an external reason or source for your assertion. A citation is when you point to a specific source that can speak on it's own with directions to what you think supports your assertion. Since we're dealing with books, the direction part is easy: state a book and a section, if not a specific passage. Then we can read it and see if your assertion is justified by the citation or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T05:06:09-07:00","id":1560022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560019#post1560019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Backed up by who? Because once again: unreliable narrator.<br /> <br /> You've got dozens of different takes about how, when and why stuff happened, and they're all shouting over each other, saying they're the right answer.<br /> <br /> Take, for example, the Rokea. They claim that their creator once possessed a magical pearl that contained the very spirit of Humanity itself within it, and that whoever possessed this pearl would thus be able to control humanity on a spiritual level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Rokea credit their existence to Kun, and making pearls is a C'et thing. The story they tell is that Qyrl stole the first pearl, which was the secret of building, for humanity, but lost some tentacles in the process when C'et shut her shell, albeit too slowly to stop the theft. C'et eventually made another pearl with the severed tentacles as a base; this was fissionable ore, and Rokea naturally take a dim view of its use in nuclear weapons. It was supposedly something that C'et ejected to avoid getting ill from it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only for the Ananasi to claim that this so called 'pearl' was actually the amber prison which Queen Ananasa has been trapped inside, and is currently in the possession of the Wyrm, after they stole it from Weaver. </div> </div> </div>Completely different and unrelated story. The Amber Prison was purpose-built for Ananasa to keep her from interfering with the Weaver, and subsequently dragged into Malfeas; the Ananasi manipulated Garou and Fera into mounting attacks on it. This succeeded only in opening up a tiny channel for Ananasa to speak to her children.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So has the biblical God of Abrahamic faiths, which is presented in both Vampire and Demon.<br /> <br /> Remember that in World of Darkness, all the various splats and their mythos exist within the same universal cosmology. Thus turning the metaplot into a gargantuan, convoluted mess.<br /> <br /> At least Chronicles had the forethought of making each splat take place within their own self contained narrative. </div> </div> </div>Werewolf didn't play ball with the others on that in Revised. The developer's assertions for the setting were that geological time and fossils were real, outer space was very much physical and continued on to the astronomical extent it does IRL, and that human belief has some serious limits on affecting the spirit world. You can see this perhaps most clearly in the Storyteller's Handbook campaign seed where it suggests possibly using space aliens (not naming them as Ka Luon or whatever, either) for a change of pace, and having them be completely ignorant of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> (And further cementing the fan assertions that the ideal Werewolf game would look like XCOM: Enemy Unknown)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My citations are the Makole and Rokea, both of whom have been roaming the earth since the time of the dinosaurs. Humanity was nowhere to be found in those ancient periods. </div> </div> </div>Before the time of the Dinosaurs (particularly for the Rokea), and in lieu of humanity they had the tool-users that were expies of Quintaglio and such. Mokole, as a matter of something we're told OOC in the description of Mnesis in their breed book, used to have Mnesis lineages that stretched back further than the Triassic, but they were wiped out in the War of Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Until the day they finally did emerge, and the Makole took on the role of Dragon Kings, helping to uplift the hairless apes from their primitive existence. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Kings&quot; was the name given to the pre-human tool-users. Dragon Kings being applied to them as a name is something done in Exalted; the name means something else in the context of the WoD, typically referring to spirits that are more familiar to the Middle Dragons.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T08:41:41-07:00","id":1560027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560022#post1560022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf didn't play ball with the others on that in Revised. The developer's assertions for the setting were that geological time and fossils were real, outer space was very much physical and continued on to the astronomical extent it does IRL, and that human belief has some serious limits on affecting the spirit world. You can see this perhaps most clearly in the Storyteller's Handbook campaign seed where it suggests possibly using space aliens (not naming them as Ka Luon or whatever, either) for a change of pace, and having them be completely ignorant of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> (And further cementing the fan assertions that the ideal Werewolf game would look like XCOM: Enemy Unknown)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I also forgot to mention that when Demons first escaped the Abyss, they had no idea who or what the Fera were, because they had no memory of ever creating them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T08:59:53-07:00","id":1560028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560021#post1560021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to be missing my point on this:</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I'm not.<br /> <br /> You're saying that your side of the discussion is backed up by what's in the book. Where as I'm pointing out the fact that the books are written from the perspective of characters that are speaking to each other in universe, and do not have access to the wealth of meta information we possess.<br /> <br /> The characters in the book are just as lost, confused, and prone to bias as the readers are. Which is why their explanation of events should be taken with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> But as for me personally, I tend to go with the worst case scenario take on the situation. Because, well, it's the World of Darkness, and the whole story is building up towards the literal end of the world in some fashion or another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560021#post1560021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What?<br /> <br /> The CofD is a single unified setting. The CofD works because it learned from the mistakes of the original WoD run and makes sure each splat as enough room to do its own thing or crossover without setting conceit issues (other issues still happen). The WoD is a mess because it started with the idea that each group was its own self-contained narrative and vampires dealt with &quot;Lupines&quot; who may or may not be the Garou. But as crossover got more popular with the fans (which also happened fast), they moved to unify the WoD as one overarching universe post hoc and that's when it got messy. And Revised tried to fix things with the bubbles-on-a-pool-cosmology but that never really caught on because only a few authors were really pushing it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not so. While there are Werewolves who appear in Requiem, or Vampires who appear in Forsaken, the books leave it nebulous as to whether or not they are the same vampires / werewolves who appear in the other games.<br /> <br /> Mage the Awakening has explicitly clarified that the Fae and Arcadia from which they draw their magic is NOT the same realm that is responsible for abducting people and turning them into Changelings.<br /> <br /> <br /> To the best of my knowledge, the only splat that was actually designed around the idea of crossover play is Beast: the Primordial... and I'm not sure anybody is even playing that anymore, after certain events came to light about its lead developer.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560021#post1560021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an appeal, not a citation. An appeal is when you point to an external reason or source for your assertion. A citation is when you point to a specific source that can speak on it's own with directions to what you think supports your assertion. Since we're dealing with books, the direction part is easy: state a book and a section, if not a specific passage. Then we can read it and see if your assertion is justified by the citation or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're saying that a couple of Fera who's existence stretched back to before the first ape slimed its way out of the primordial gene pool isn't citation of just how long the Triat has been up to their shenanigans?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T12:37:33-07:00","id":1560030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560027#post1560027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also forgot to mention that when Demons first escaped the Abyss, they had no idea who or what the Fera were, because they had no memory of ever creating them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the point of bringing it up? Do you think Saur Ops or I don't know that the WoD is an incoherent mess of contradictory narratives if you smash all the different games together? What does presenting more evidence of this do?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560028#post1560028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I'm not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yes, you are, because you're response is not accurate to what I've been saying. If something I'm saying is hurting communication please try to highlight it, but I'm not really sure where you're getting certain conclusions from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're saying that your side of the discussion is backed up by what's in the book. </div> </div> </div>OK, there's two different issues here:<br /> <br /> 1) I think we need to not just cite the books (re: unreliable narrator) but provide reasons for why we're citing what we are. The quotes I cited from W20 core? Those are 3rd person sections. That's the authors speaking directly to the audience, not the authors speaking through a character with biases. My reasoning is that it's what the creators want us to consider the base-line, not the stuff that is supposed to be up to in-game disagreement that various groups can have legitimate differences on. We're getting the bare bones of &quot;these are the essential basics of the Triat, and here's where things get interpreted by different groups,&quot; which I feel is a compelling starting point on what attributes the Triat ought to be assigned out-of-character (or &quot;meta&quot;) instead of what needs to be inferred form unreliable narrators.<br /> <br /> 2) You seem to not be taking the level of disagreement as a reason to go back to the books and make sure you're getting your info right. Our memories are fallible. I completely forgot about the Ananasi book's whole telling of the origin of the setting until Saur Ops brought it up. I probably would have phrased things differently if I hadn't forgotten she goes into the Weaver making the moon barren (esp. because that version doesn't follow your conclusions from it). You brought up the need for canon... but what's the point of looking to the canon if you're not going to actively consult it to make sure you're making the best possible points?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The characters in the book are just as lost, confused, and prone to bias as the readers are. Which is why their explanation of events should be taken with a grain of salt. </div> </div> </div>But you're not applying this to your own points. You did not say, &quot;according to some stories the moon is barren because Luna pissed off a Triat member, and this is why we should accept that as true over taking it with a grain of salt.&quot; You just asserted that the moon is barren in WtA because Luna pissed of a Triat member, and the backlash was so bad it impacted every moon in the whole cosmos. That's the gap I'm trying to point at in your statements that I think you need to address.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But as for me personally, I tend to go with the worst case scenario take on the situation. Because, well, it's the World of Darkness, and the whole story is building up towards the literal end of the world in some fashion or another. </div> </div> </div>Then why are you appealing the age of the Mokole and Rokea? Gaia being above the Triat is far worse a scenario than Gaia being below the Triat. If Gaia is dying, and she's above the Triat, her death is cosmically catastrophic. If Gaia is below the Triat, they could in theory make a similar entity at some point later. It would be apocalyptic for everything on Earth, but it's not a threat the whole universe as long as the Triat persist. <br /> <br /> And honestly, if your goal is to just establish what the worst case scenario is, that should be it's own thread so people can participate towards helping you towards that specific goal rather than something here where we're discussing the same subject with different goals. I'm looking for the most well support interpretation of the WtA cosmology because that makes it the most useful for broad ranging forum discussions like &quot;what happens when moving a character from how the cosmology in W20 works into W5 and it's different cosmology.&quot; The worst case isn't wrong to establish, but it's not useful for most other discussions in a general fan group because few discussions are going to assume that interpretation is the one to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not so. </div> </div> </div>Yes, very much so. Your trivia factoids don't really address the differences in design at all.<br /> <br /> The CofD allows the games to be siloed, yes, but all of the games are written so they can crossover without cosmological level snarls. The Astral Realm is mostly explored by mages in the CofD, but lots of supernaturals can get there, and it's the same Realm with the same rules for everybody. The same is true of the other Realms like the Hedge/Arcadia or the Underworld/Lower Depths, or the Hisil/Shadow/Primodrial Wilds. The setting is constant between the game lines even if the gamelines do not all equally focus on all parts of the setting. A werewolf might never even learn the Primordial Dream exists, let alone that its part of the Astral Realm, but if a werewolf does that can interact with it without there being some vast challenge to the metaphysics of werewolves in the game. That's what the CofD learned from the complexity of trying to merge every non-material Realm in the WoD into falling under the one giant umbrella of the Umbra.<br /> <br /> The most common metaphysical paradoxes in the CofD are there by design to keep the Supernal Realms of Awakening from overriding everyone else like WoD Demon did; if mages bring Supernal things into the Fallen World... they get scrambled in a fashion that denies any ability to prove what the &quot;truth&quot; actually is. <br /> <br /> The whole of the CofD was designed with crossover in mind. Beast was special in that it was the only game where crossover is a core part of the main game play loop. The other games are designed so crossover can work if groups want to do it. Beast was designed for groups that expect crossover to happen in the game as a regular part of the story (and even then you don't actually have do, it's just a dick move to not tell your group if you plan to run Beast without crossover so they don't invest in various traits).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, you're saying that a couple of Fera who's existence stretched back to before the first ape slimed its way out of the primordial gene pool isn't citation of just how long the Triat has been up to their shenanigans? </div> </div> </div>Yes. It's still an appeal. You're just appealing to the supposed age of the groups without justifying why that makes them reliable (plenty of stuff contradicts their stories too), and you're not citing specific things they say that actually supports your broader positions.<br /> <br /> Like I said, discussing stuff with this much uncertainty created by the source texts themselves requires actual reasoning so we're not just asserting interpretations at each other uselessly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T14:16:54-07:00","id":1560032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560030#post1560030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the point of bringing it up? Do you think Saur Ops or I don't know that the WoD is an incoherent mess of contradictory narratives if you smash all the different games together? What does presenting more evidence of this do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, how the hell is this difficult for you to comprehend?<br /> <br /> <b>The point</b> is me trying to show you that any such claims about who's the strongest, or who created what first, or who represent what in the grand cosmology, is totally up in the air. Because World of Darkness chose to give us 'suggestions' instead of hard confirmation.<br /> <br /> Did Gaia create the universe and the Triat?<br /> <br /> According to the Fera, yes.<br /> <br /> According to Vampires and Demons, no.<br /> <br /> Vampire say that God created it, while Demons say that it was a collaborative effort they carried out under his orders.<br /> <br /> So, again, <b>unreliable narrator.</b> If you read a passage that came from the mouth of an in universe character, then anything they say can neither be confirmed or denied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T16:14:20-07:00","id":1560034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560032#post1560032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, how the hell is this difficult for you to comprehend?</div> </div> </div> </div>The part where you think I'm the one doing what you're complaining about when you're the one guilty of it.<br /> <br /> I qualified a post as the &quot;traditional Gaian default as presented in the books,&quot; and you countered with, &quot;No, that's wrong, here's the object truth,&quot; and your counter to me questioning your objective statements is, &quot;Unreliable narrator means whatever I say is correct and whatever you say is wrong.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you read a passage that came from the mouth of an in universe character, then anything they say can neither be confirmed or denied. </div> </div> </div><b>Which is why I quoted THE AUTHORS not a character in my post.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T18:24:46-07:00","id":1560036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560027#post1560027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also forgot to mention that when Demons first escaped the Abyss, they had no idea who or what the Fera were, because they had no memory of ever creating them.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>More points for &quot;fuck Demon, it doesn't know shit&quot;, then. Which is just telling Vampire the same thing by proxy, if it insists on carrying that Noddist torch all night, every night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The point</b> is me trying to show you that any such claims about who's the strongest, or who created what first, or who represent what in the grand cosmology, is totally up in the air. Because World of Darkness chose to give us 'suggestions' instead of hard confirmation. </div> </div> </div>This would be a much more believable thesis if you had actually read the books. YouTube lore dumps flavored with headcanon are no substitute for sitting down and taking in the years worth of WoD material.<br /> <br /> Well, the years worth of Werewolf, anyway. Not so sure that V:tM is worth the time.<br /> <br /> /jk<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did Gaia create the universe and the Triat? </div> </div> </div>Gaia may be the universe and the Triat on a higher level of organization, and, again, may always have just existed. And ultimately, acts of &quot;creation&quot; don't really matter. Demon trying to act like it made everything, out of order of how shit actually came into being, is just Christian wankery about trying to look like the big dog in a religious horror setting. And Werewolf is neither a religious horror setting, nor a personal horror setting; bring the demons and the vampires into a crossover game, watch them turn into stuff on a rock, by one of the enemies of the Garou and Fera if not by one of the Garou or Fera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> According to the Fera, yes.<br /> <br /> According to Vampires and Demons, no.<br /> <br /> Vampire say that God created it, while Demons say that it was a collaborative effort they carried out under his orders. </div> </div> </div>Quoth the Werewolf Revised Storyteller's Handbook, &quot;Not everything needs to be shackled to Vampire mythology, you know.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, again, <b>unreliable narrator.</b> If you read a passage that came from the mouth of an in universe character, then anything they say can neither be confirmed or denied. </div> </div> </div>Except when Revised came around and said &quot;No, actually, this IS how things are&quot; for a lot of stuff.<br /> <br /> Bastet regarding Garou as delulu about the need to fight the Wyrm? Well, the Wyrm is encroaching on everyone, let's see them gamecraft their way out of that. Nuwisha and Corax exploring the Umbra? They're back, and shit's getting grim, especially since a special breed of bane is devoted just to hunting down the former. Also, they're supporting the importance of whatever last stand everyone else is going to make. Ajaba? Completely retconned in Revised to be one of the central players of the Ahadi and not a Lion King retread. Ratkin swearing at Gaia? Not something that was done nearly so much after the end of things started rolling in.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Mokole didn't even wait until Revised. It was still 2e and asserted that Mage's Umbra was, by and large, not to be used in a Werewolf game.<br /> <br /> So while there's a fairly generous amount of wiggle room overall, Revised definitely had starker divisions between the games and let them do their own thing. Which is kind of necessary to enjoy some of the &quot;smaller&quot; details of the game and stop navel gazing about how created the world or even if it was, maybe it was always just here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T19:59:46-07:00","id":1560037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560036#post1560036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More points for &quot;fuck Demon, it doesn't know shit&quot;, then. Which is just telling Vampire the same thing by proxy, if it insists on carrying that Noddist torch all night, every night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon also tries to tell us human souls were never sent to Hell, and it was reserved specifically for the rebellious angels. But then we have people like the Kuei-Jin, who are supposed to be the souls of those who got sent to hell, but managed to escape and possess a dead body. THEN we have Wraiths, who claim your soul ends up in the Shadowlands upon death, while any interpretations of the afterlife have become pale, corrupted versions of what humans envisioned.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560036#post1560036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would be a much more believable thesis if you had actually read the books. YouTube lore dumps flavored with headcanon are no substitute for sitting down and taking in the years worth of WoD material.<br /> <br /> Well, the years worth of Werewolf, anyway. Not so sure that V:tM is worth the time.<br /> <br /> /jk</div> </div> </div> </div>The lore dumps I watch are from people who are actually discussing the books, instead of advertising them. They'll even post screenshots taken directly from the book to show what they're talking about.<br /> <br /> Problem is just that I have a crap memory, and a lot of these videos are over an hour long.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560036#post1560036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gaia may be the universe and the Triat on a higher level of organization, and, again, may always have just existed. And ultimately, acts of &quot;creation&quot; don't really matter. Demon trying to act like it made everything, out of order of how shit actually came into being, is just Christian wankery about trying to look like the big dog in a religious horror setting. And Werewolf is neither a religious horror setting, nor a personal horror setting; bring the demons and the vampires into a crossover game, watch them turn into stuff on a rock, by one of the enemies of the Garou and Fera if not by one of the Garou or Fera.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Quoth the Werewolf Revised Storyteller's Handbook, &quot;Not everything needs to be shackled to Vampire mythology, you know.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Demons are quite possibly the most powerful splat in World of Darkness. There's a reason why the End Times kicked off shortly after they managed to escape from the Abyss. It's because they were far too powerful to have been walking around outside of an apocalyptic level event.<br /> <br /> A demon's overall strength depends upon how much faith they are able to harvest. In theory, if they are able to collect enough of it, they could become as powerful as God himself. Which is basically what the Faustians are trying to achieve by making pacts with mortals to expand their cults.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, if Gaia is the spirit of the universe, and she's dead... then, that's it.<br /> <br /> Pack it up.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi won.<br /> <br /> Except that not only is the universe not dissolving into a swirling mass of primordial chaos, but humanity doesn't even seem to notice her absence.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-16T23:55:16-07:00","id":1560040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560037#post1560037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demon also tries to tell us human souls were never sent to Hell, and it was reserved specifically for the rebellious angels. But then we have people like the Kuei-Jin, who are supposed to be the souls of those who got sent to hell, but managed to escape and possess a dead body. THEN we have Wraiths, who claim your soul ends up in the Shadowlands upon death, while any interpretations of the afterlife have become pale, corrupted versions of what humans envisioned.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot to include Malfeas as a Hell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The lore dumps I watch are from people who are actually discussing the books, instead of advertising them. They'll even post screenshots taken directly from the book to show what they're talking about. </div> </div> </div>Every big WoD head has a lens to spin things with. Notably, your coming in here and being utterly adamant about how the WoD is totally stuck together and unified.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problem is just that I have a crap memory, and a lot of these videos are over an hour long. </div> </div> </div>And you're coming in here to tell us you're wrong equipped as such because...?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons are quite possibly the most powerful splat in World of Darkness. There's a reason why the End Times kicked off shortly after they managed to escape from the Abyss. It's because they were far too powerful to have been walking around outside of an apocalyptic level event.<br /> <br /> A demon's overall strength depends upon how much faith they are able to harvest. In theory, if they are able to collect enough of it, they could become as powerful as God himself. Which is basically what the Faustians are trying to achieve by making pacts with mortals to expand their cults. </div> </div> </div>It's rather telling that Werewolf continued giving D:tF the cold shoulder even with W20. Its Antagonists chapter, much like in Revised, continues to not acknowledge the existence of D:tF, whereas V20 has Demons that are absolutely the same as in D:tF statted in shorthand. M20 gives them some time in the shadow folk countermagick section, Wr20 has a might-be in the Angelic and Demonics, and C20 has demons as a type of prodigal, but W20 flat out says &quot;No, fuck you, get out.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't be powerful if you flat out don't exist and no one cared to even make the most bare bones crossover rules. One can also reasonably assume if you're playing W:tA that nothing from D:tF will be used, or else is so close to being a bane that it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if Gaia is the spirit of the universe, and she's dead... then, that's it. </div> </div> </div>That is why W5 is all 6s and 7s, yes. Well, one reason of many.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pack it up.<br /> <br /> The Nephandi won. </div> </div> </div>...Your first thought is going to a Mage antagonist? A character type from a game that's almost as at odds with W:tA as Demon is, and believes about the exact opposite of what W:tA does? None of this matters for a Mage game. Mages almost certainly aren't going to exist the way you read them if you're playing Werewolf, and vice versa.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that not only is the universe not dissolving into a swirling mass of primordial chaos, but humanity doesn't even seem to notice her absence. </div> </div> </div>That's Mage's thing. That is why you can't really say that the WoD is a singular, unified setting. If you did decide to run crossover, and you are trying to answer these high-level setting questions, you have to make an executive decision as ST as to who is actually right, and it has to be one or the other. They don't play well together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T05:29:42-07:00","id":1560041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560040#post1560040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You forgot to include Malfeas as a Hell.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's a werewolf hell, primarily used for bad doggos, who shit on Gaia's carpet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560040#post1560040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's rather telling that Werewolf continued giving D:tF the cold shoulder even with W20. Its Antagonists chapter, much like in Revised, continues to not acknowledge the existence of D:tF, whereas V20 has Demons that are absolutely the same as in D:tF statted in shorthand. M20 gives them some time in the shadow folk countermagick section, Wr20 has a might-be in the Angelic and Demonics, and C20 has demons as a type of prodigal, but W20 flat out says &quot;No, fuck you, get out.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't be powerful if you flat out don't exist and no one cared to even make the most bare bones crossover rules. One can also reasonably assume if you're playing W:tA that nothing from D:tF will be used, or else is so close to being a bane that it doesn't matter.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but was it not the Garou who imprisoned Kupala within the Carpathian Mountains?<br /> <br /> Which would mean they are directly responsible for the creation of an earthbound?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560040#post1560040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's Mage's thing. That is why you can't really say that the WoD is a singular, unified setting. If you did decide to run crossover, and you are trying to answer these high-level setting questions, you have to make an executive decision as ST as to who is actually right, and it has to be one or the other. They don't play well together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the one saying that. The metaplot is.<br /> <br /> Also, you can't say that Mage isn't involved, since it's pretty established that the Kindred and the Garou have clashed in the past. That means the Tremere exist within Werewolf, and if they exist, then the Order of Hermes would also exist, which means so do the Nine Mystic Traditions. If I'm not mistaken (correct me if I am), Samuel learned about the Skinwalker ritual from the Verbena, and also sought to become an Awakened mage himself.<br /> <br /> And I agree that the metaplot contradicts itself at every turn. Which is why White Wolf were right to end it all and reboot the franchise from scratch.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T09:44:57-07:00","id":1560045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560009#post1560009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about restraint. It's about the practical reality on the ground for the Garou of W5. Without the Garou Nation (and OOC with the massive nerf they took via their mental health tracks), they have no way to organize mass scale revolutions against humanity; esp. a newly empowered technological and aware-of-the-supernatural government lead humanity.<br /> <br /> As I said, W5 is a whimper of an apocalypse. The time and ability to make the kind of difference you're talking about has passed already. As it stands in W5, a movement to &quot;go loud&quot; is just going to get shut down by silver bullet armed spec ops soldiers before it can do anything that can't be covered up.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's something that I think the writers of 5th edition have massively overlooked in regards to trying to present the SI as a legitimate threat. Vampires may need to actively work to cover up a breach of the masquerade, but the Garou have Delirium, while Changelings have The Mists.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter how advanced their technology is in the modern era, they're still susceptible to the genetically inherited PTSD that is Delirium. You send in an SI strike team against a pack of werewolves, and they're going to be reduced to screaming, quivering heaps, as they collapse into a puddle of their own urine.<br /> <br /> Even those rare individuals who have the willpower to respond with aggression do so in a manic, frenzied state. Hardly the kind of mental state necessary to be carrying out a coordinated assault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T10:23:07-07:00","id":1560046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560041#post1560041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a werewolf hell, primarily used for bad doggos, who shit on Gaia's carpet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hence, a hell. Incidentally, CoD would also eventually be extemely coy about what &quot;real&quot; hell was.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Correct me if I'm wrong, but was it not the Garou who imprisoned Kupala within the Carpathian Mountains?<br /> <br /> Which would mean they are directly responsible for the creation of an earthbound? </div> </div> </div>Every Earthbound previously mentioned in lore is only an Earthbound because of a carpet-pulling, climax-ruining retcon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not the one saying that. The metaplot is. </div> </div> </div>So, this is important to note, but there is not &quot;the&quot; metaplot. There was one for each game, and Werewolf had one that was actually very, very light and sparse. Black Tooth got killed, but no one knows who did it, so the PCs could do it. The Stargazers left the Garou Nation for the Beast Courts, but a lot of them still stuck around in the packs they had been a part of. Albrecht got the Silver Crown and destroyed the Seventh Generation, but he didn't manage to perform the assault that killed them alone.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Vampire metaplot was dumb, heavy-handed, and purposefully overshadowed any PCs at every opportunity. No one would want to be a part of that, so it's understandable that the worst offender eventually became the rallying cry for getting rid of everything, even though it didn't touch every game the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you can't say that Mage isn't involved, since it's pretty established that the Kindred and the Garou have clashed in the past. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I can, and also the Garou didn't necessarily clash with Kindred. They clashed with vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That means the Tremere exist within Werewolf, and if they exist, then the Order of Hermes would also exist, which means so do the Nine Mystic Traditions. If I'm not mistaken (correct me if I am), Samuel learned about the Skinwalker ritual from the Verbena, and also sought to become an Awakened mage himself. </div> </div> </div>Sam learned in somewhere in India, back in a time when Mage was an extremely tentative game concept, since it was in Valkenburg Foundation and a lot of things hadn't been established then. Later, W20 would detail how it originated with the kin of the Balam and made its way around the world.<br /> <br /> (You might be confusing this with how Sam later stole a Verbena relic that allowed him to use Special K and ignore Paradox until so much built up that he exploded in The Chaos Factor. After he also tried to eat a power field larger than his head by hitting the El Dorado realm with the Conquistador's Sword in Rage Across the Amazon. Yeah, there's a reason that Sam Haight is only interesting when he's mentioned in the context of Werewolf.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I agree that the metaplot contradicts itself at every turn. Which is why White Wolf were right to end it all and reboot the franchise from scratch. </div> </div> </div>Again, there isn't a single metaplot. It was a bunch of smaller ones that often got ignored because Vampire and Demon were covering the bed with censor-worthy levels of bloody diarrhea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T14:47:01-07:00","id":1560047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560046#post1560046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And hence, a hell. Incidentally, CoD would also eventually be extemely coy about what &quot;real&quot; hell was.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because CoD is more of an open world sandbox, where each chronicle is meant to be its own stand alone adventure. They only connect to each other if the Storyteller wants them to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560046#post1560046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, this is important to note, but there is not &quot;the&quot; metaplot. There was one for each game, and Werewolf had one that was actually very, very light and sparse. Black Tooth got killed, but no one knows who did it, so the PCs could do it. The Stargazers left the Garou Nation for the Beast Courts, but a lot of them still stuck around in the packs they had been a part of. Albrecht got the Silver Crown and destroyed the Seventh Generation, but he didn't manage to perform the assault that killed them alone.<br /> <br /> In contrast, the Vampire metaplot was dumb, heavy-handed, and purposefully overshadowed any PCs at every opportunity. No one would want to be a part of that, so it's understandable that the worst offender eventually became the rallying cry for getting rid of everything, even though it didn't touch every game the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not aware of that. I thought the Metaplot was an attempt to tie everything together into one interconnected story. But that does help clarify why it's so extremely contradictory.<br /> <br /> ((That's just how vampire society works. <i>&quot;Fuck over anyone who's less than 300 years old, and then blame them when things go south!&quot;</i>))<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560046#post1560046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sam learned in somewhere in India, back in a time when Mage was an extremely tentative game concept, since it was in Valkenburg Foundation and a lot of things hadn't been established then. Later, W20 would detail how it originated with the kin of the Balam and made its way around the world.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He was also a meme, intended to make fun of power gamers that wanted to stack splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T17:49:47-07:00","id":1560050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560047#post1560047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's because CoD is more of an open world sandbox, where each chronicle is meant to be its own stand alone adventure. They only connect to each other if the Storyteller wants them to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's just because WW was chronically edgy until about the 2010s and wanted to keep using demons and &quot;hell&quot; for said edge. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was not aware of that. I thought the Metaplot was an attempt to tie everything together into one interconnected story. But that does help clarify why it's so extremely contradictory.<br /> <br /> ((That's just how vampire society works. <i>&quot;Fuck over anyone who's less than 300 years old, and then blame them when things go south!&quot;</i>)) </div> </div> </div>Especially when Revised hit and each game was re-dedicated to doing things its own way, with its own themes, and to the specifications of its own particular developer. Mage might have been hit by the Avatar Storm, but this was not a thing in W:tA; anything involving the Week of Nightmares was kept very loose, and its exact significance to vampires hazy; and sometimes Caine was compared to the Eater-of-Souls, but more as a bone thrown to V:tM in hypothetical crossover scenarios than anything else. &quot;You want to play in this game? Great, we're giving you a place under one of the most rapacious, detestable forces in the setting that was originally involved in the soulless, greedy expansion of colonialism. Have fun.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He was also a meme, intended to make fun of power gamers that wanted to stack splats. </div> </div> </div>The 90s were a time when balancing concerns weren't really well considered and a lot of D&amp;D's in-game vindictiveness by practice had yet to be purged. Sam wouldn't really be done nowadays, not just because of the general ironclad rule of &quot;only one type&quot; but also because the writers eventually realized that concerns like this should really be handled out of character and not by saying &quot;alright, you've arbitrarily reached a point that I'm going to screw you over on in spite of putting up with your shit up to here. Your character is now only one character type - a ghost.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then, of course, he became soulsteel, and then an ashtray. Which beaned a character in the Mage ToJ novel when a bunch of debris from the Underworld got swept in from a Tempest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-17T22:12:33-07:00","id":1560052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quo