 going to screw you over on in spite of putting up with your shit up to here. Your character is now only one character type - a ghost.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, but I might want to play an Abomination some day!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 05-18-2026, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T00:17:15-07:00","id":1560055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560052#post1560052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What you call <i>&quot;edgy&quot;</i> - the 90's called<i> &quot;rule of cool!&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would you have preferred I called it a cheap cash-in on In Nomine?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aww, but I might want to play an Abomination some day! </div> </div> </div>Enjoy your chronically halved dice pools! And being taken out after your first lapse against Gaia if you're homid-born and didn't buy dots in Gnosis!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T02:54:13-07:00","id":1560058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560055#post1560055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you have preferred I called it a cheap cash-in on In Nomine?</div> </div> </div> </div>It gave us epic shit like Sgt. Rage using one hand to tear the roof off a panzer tank, while using his other arm to fire an M60 into the operator.<br /> <br /> As well as Golgol Fangs-First, who's dual wielding miniguns in the fight for the Amazon Rainforest.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's undeniably edgy. But it's also rad AF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T05:01:18-07:00","id":1560059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560058#post1560058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It gave us epic shit like Sgt. Rage using one hand to tear the roof off a panzer tank, while using his other arm to fire an M60 into the operator.<br /> <br /> As well as Golgol Fangs-First, who's dual wielding miniguns in the fight for the Amazon Rainforest.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it's undeniably edgy. But it's also rad AF.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which is related to D:tF and its &quot;if you weren't practicing an Abrahamic religion you're worshiping a demon!&quot; BS (and other BS related to demons).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T06:56:31-07:00","id":1560060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560059#post1560059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> None of which is related to D:tF and its &quot;if you weren't practicing an Abrahamic religion you're worshiping a demon!&quot; BS (and other BS related to demons).</div> </div> </div> </div>From a real world stand point, I fully agree that accusing non-Abrahamic faiths as being demon worship is idiotic bullshit. Especially when some of them predate the Abrahamic faiths by a few millennia.<br /> <br /> But within the context of the game, I work with the material provided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-18T12:49:47-07:00","id":1560073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560060#post1560060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a real world stand point, I fully agree that accusing non-Abrahamic faiths as being demon worship is idiotic bullshit. Especially when some of them predate the Abrahamic faiths by a few millennia.<br /> <br /> But within the context of the game, I work with the material provided.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's only in within the context for Demon. Demon, the johnny come lately that asserted that it could put order to everything and explain it all sensibly. (Spoilers: see the xkcd competing standards comic for how that worked out.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T00:26:01-07:00","id":1560085,"title":"","content":"To get things back on topic, I'm pretty sure the whole baggage carried across the editions (As the posts above has shown) prompted Minds eye theater to make Version of WtA is a setting Reset since it starts with a (Probably not The) Apocalypse happened, which among other things killed off a good chunk of the past editions Metaplot characters and blew up most of the Cearns. Which leaves a sandbox for ST to fill in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T01:11:22-07:00","id":1560086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560085#post1560085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To get things back on topic, I'm pretty sure the whole baggage carried across the editions (As the posts above has shown) prompted Minds eye theater to make Version of WtA is a setting Reset since it starts with a (Probably not The) Apocalypse happened, which among other things killed off a good chunk of the past editions Metaplot characters and blew up most of the Cearns. Which leaves a sandbox for ST to fill in.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole point of the Rokea's existence, was that Gaia anticipated the Garou were going to fail, so she made them as a backup plan. Once the dust settles, the Rokea are supposed to repopulate the planet.<br /> <br /> Which is why it's not considered dishonorable for them to flee combat. They aren't supposed to go down swinging, they were supposed to live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-19T02:20:54-07:00","id":1560087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1560086#post1560086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The whole point of the Rokea's existence, was that Gaia anticipated the Garou were going to fail, so she made them as a backup plan. Once the dust settles, the Rokea are supposed to repopulate the planet.<br /> <br /> Which is why it's not considered dishonorable for them to flee combat. They aren't supposed to go down swinging, they were supposed to live.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean to be fair the apocalypse Prsented in the BNS version Isn't Proprer Apocalypse partly due to King Albrecht sacrificing himself to stop it. Like besides the cearns being blown up and the emergence of the bitten. There isn't much fallout from the apocalypse, to the point that it's totally unknown to the mundane world beyond some freak weather events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T13:03:21-07:00","id":1562236,"title":"","content":"A W20 Garou thrown in W5 would... Change nothing.<br /> <br /> They'd probably dedicate their time to find a way back home, where they're needed.<br /> <br /> If for some reason they decide to stay, they'd be only one. A strong fella, probably, but only one.<br /> <br /> W5 changing in response to the presence of a W20 Garou is another proposal entirely, not a logically reachable conclusion to the premise. Or would the opposite happen, and a W5 Garou in W20 make by sheer presence the Universe change in a metaphysical level?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T18:35:06-07:00","id":1562245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562236#post1562236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A W20 Garou thrown in W5 would... Change nothing.<br /> <br /> They'd probably dedicate their time to find a way back home, where they're needed.<br /> <br /> If for some reason they decide to stay, they'd be only one. A strong fella, probably, but only one.<br /> <br /> W5 changing in response to the presence of a W20 Garou is another proposal entirely, not a logically reachable conclusion to the premise. Or would the opposite happen, and a W5 Garou in W20 make by sheer presence the Universe change in a metaphysical level?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to think that a W5 Garou in a legacy world would be like that one alternate Dandy in Space Dandy that has the freakish, non-helmet wearing Meow and the QT that's just some old guy in a space suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T00:58:05-07:00","id":1562248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562236#post1562236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A W20 Garou thrown in W5 would... Change nothing.<br /> <br /> They'd probably dedicate their time to find a way back home, where they're needed.<br /> <br /> If for some reason they decide to stay, they'd be only one. A strong fella, probably, but only one.</div> </div> </div> </div>One person, who wields powers that can theoretically go all the way up to demigod level capabilities.<br /> <br /> Displaced into a setting that is trying to keep the power system down to street level.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T04:09:14-07:00","id":1562250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562248#post1562248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One person, who wields powers that can theoretically go all the way up to demigod level capabilities.<br /> <br /> Displaced into a setting that is trying to keep the power system down to street level.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, big deal.<br /> <br /> Whatever they decide to do, they'll be really good at it in comparison. IF we assume every single advantage survives the isekai journey, and that they're Rank 4+.<br /> <br /> Still only one. Not going to solo entire Septs at once. Not going to have an infinite Gnosis or Rage battery. Not going to survive a sustained onslaught if push comes to shove.<br /> <br /> This is not about being the strongest, is about scale. The character can do a lot of interesting things, arguably far more interesting than just changing the world to show off. But changing the world just by virtue of being strong is not a reasonable expectation.<br /> <br /> I think this exercise is actually valid and really interesting if taken seriously, as hard as it may be to take W5 seriously, but it's actually doable. I think there's a lot of interesting stories to be told about a W20 Garou transported to a world where the Wyrm won and the remains of the Nation fight to have a less shitty demise rather than saving the planet. A world where Gaia is dead.<br /> <br /> But the OP idea of a single character derailing a whole setting assumptions and structures by being &quot;unbalanced&quot;? That's bullshit and purely <br /> childish tantrum over a petty frustration with the new setting.<br /> <br /> Paradox made an awful job with W5, yes, we all know that. It's badly written AND disrespectful with fans, dully noted.<br /> <br /> Disparaging the fictional proposal at every opportunity for narrow-minded self-gratification disguised as thought exercise isn't better or more interesting, it's actually less. As far as the declared purpose of this thread goes, nothing would change in a big scale.<br /> <br /> A lot of more interesting questions on such a scenario exist:<br /> - How would those characters translate mechanically?<br /> - Who's the guest? Tribe, Sept, Auspice, Breed...<br /> - Is the journey sudden or long? Deliberate or accidental? Do they know they're in another world rather than another time?<br /> - What actually makes sense to be transferred? Totem bonuses? Gifts? Rank?<br /> - How they understand this place, their reason to be there and the local werewolves?<br /> - How they arrive? How are they received?<br /> - What interesting goals we can set to this character in an objective, measurable manner, so that any performance analysis can actually makes sense.<br /> <br /> For now no one flags this thread because no one really liked the new setting, if not for the reasons you think. But this is edition warring for the sake of it, which is both against the rules of the forum and boring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T07:00:50-07:00","id":1562257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562250#post1562250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, big deal.<br /> <br /> Whatever they decide to do, they'll be really good at it in comparison. IF we assume every single advantage survives the isekai journey, and that they're Rank 4+.<br /> <br /> Still only one. Not going to solo entire Septs at once. Not going to have an infinite Gnosis or Rage battery. Not going to survive a sustained onslaught if push comes to shove.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;There's no kill like overkill.&quot;</i> - That single Garou doesn't need to concern themselves with overwhelming numbers, when they have the power to conjure a flash flood, or a category 5 tornado. Nobody is going to be sticking around to settle a physical dispute after they whip out that card. And the one who do will become a fine example of natural selection at work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T12:45:13-07:00","id":1562270,"title":"","content":"I feel like, given the completely undefined aspects of what it porting from legacy to W5 or back fully entails, there's a lot of overstating on either side.<br /> <br /> A high level W20 Garou in W5 is not going to struggle taking down &quot;Septs&quot; because W5 doesn't have the large level 5 Caerns with associated large Sept communities guarding them any more. Most Septs are just a pack or two and some kin. The higher level &quot;room nuke&quot; powers in W20 can address the numerical disadvantages (as can possibly things like summoning groups of high level spirits to aid them in combat... but again are those W20 spirits or W5 spirits?). But the decentralization also minimizes the kind of impact that can effectively have. Taking over a few small Caerns by crushing a few packs... makes you a local badass and then what? You haven't really changed the world in any meaningful way. You ability to turn that local power base into a bigger force for disruption only matters if you can start to translate W20 powers to W5 characters to start to build up a following of Garou that have a reason to join your cause instead of just avoiding you.<br /> <br /> If you're stuck going alone, eventually the numbers issue will go beyond what even high level W20 PCs can mitigate because W5 Garou will gang up in bigger and bigger numbers the more of a threat your W20 monster poses. Recruiting W5 Garou that are stuck being W5 Garou can delay this, but eventually the opposition to one tyrannical Garou of immense power with overwhelm getting some followers if they're stuck at W5 Garou power scaling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T13:46:46-07:00","id":1562275,"title":"","content":"A W20 Garou can definitely disrupt things further, but in the same sense any PC can. Their plans and behavior as a character will matter far more than their power level.<br /> <br /> Some will depend a lot on the setting itself. This Garou is not in their world anymore and we've been sidestepping, but now I think is a good moment to face the reality that coming with everything they have there isn't likely. They are in W5 world now, and have to follow W5 assumptions to some degree.<br /> <br /> For starters, what do the Spirits think of them? And what they get from the Umbra itself? The spirits could very well be wary of this interloper as what they truly is: an unknown alien entire. They look like the local werewolves, but isn't.<br /> <br /> Rank 0 is likely as they have no recognition here. Gifts and Rituals that rely on calling spirits also fail. Rituals in general are open to debate. Gifts I think would mostly remain, but not unchanged.<br /> <br /> Everything concerning Garou society is gone. No Pure Breed, no Sept, no Tribe. No, your tribe's &quot;equivalent&quot; is not really the same. It is not the same social construct, just a semantic echo so to speak. No Totem of any kind.<br /> <br /> The only known spirits available are any bound in a Fetish they brought, but those will face the same unknown, potentially hostile environment.<br /> <br /> We're talking an Umbra that dishes Aggravated damage into local Garou just by being there. What can it do to the interloper? I for one think such a game would be way more interesting, and more believable, if they got a heavy fall in power until they manage to rebuild the context for their abilities to exist in the new world. And the very possibility of saving the world is still up in the air, since Gaia is dead and in thesis not replaceable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T14:06:59-07:00","id":1562277,"title":"","content":"Less sidestepping and more that the OP addressed this much earlier in the thread that the point was to assume that questions fall in the W20 Garou's favor. That's why I stressed how big of a deal it would be if they could &quot;convert&quot; W5 Garou into W20 Garou in terms of how big of an impact they could have. The W20 character gets W20 Umbra rules, W20 spirit rules, etc. by the conceit of the thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-28T15:00:43-07:00","id":1562281,"title":"","content":"But in this situation, if taken seriously, the W20 Garou would be the least disruptive thing wandering around, given that they're bringing with them a whole cosmology.<br /> <br /> It's sidestepping in the sense that no one proposed how that works to begin with, so I'm pulling this matter now and proposing an actual playable scenario. Anyone is welcome to propose a scenario where they have everything in their favor rather than just stating they have.<br /> <br /> This is no detail, because that requires the whole support system that makes the W20 Garou work would also interact with W5. There is no W20 Garou in full power without the W20 setting behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T00:51:13-07:00","id":1562288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562270#post1562270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're stuck going alone, eventually the numbers issue will go beyond what even high level W20 PCs can mitigate because W5 Garou will gang up in bigger and bigger numbers the more of a threat your W20 monster poses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Will they? Because W5 makes it sound like the Garou nation has collapsed, and the former members are running around like headless chickens, desperately trying to figure out what their next move is going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T03:23:35-07:00","id":1562295,"title":"","content":"It doesn't exactly take a highly coordinated force to realize a big enough threat is taking over big areas to the point where the only sensible option is to attack in huge numbers. Given the number of normally solitary animals IRL that can figure this out, it's not exactly a big stretch that some werewolves can get there eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T03:43:12-07:00","id":1562296,"title":"","content":"<br /> If we even get to this point.<br /> <br /> Given they're only one person, it's literally impossible for this werewolf to really control a large area, assuming all they have going for themselves is being stronger.<br /> <br /> Their power only goes as far as their arms. To submit a Sept they have to leave the current one, to punish someone they have to get there.<br /> <br /> Changing the world would require being a good administrator and coordinator, having support, and several other things unrelated to strength. A leader can definitely use combat prowess as a tool to gather attention and respect, but one that really has only that to go for, not going to achieve much, if anything.<br /> <br /> A very likely possibility is that... Others will just stay away from them and you'll have a solitary monster inhabiting a Caern, the end. All they do is keep a few miles of abandoned land.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T07:43:57-07:00","id":1562304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562296#post1562296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we even get to this point.<br /> <br /> Given they're only one person, it's literally impossible for this werewolf to really control a large area, assuming all they have going for themselves is being stronger.<br /> <br /> Their power only goes as far as their arms. To submit a Sept they have to leave the current one, to punish someone they have to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;You may be as powerful as an army, but you can't be in as many places as one.&quot;</i> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> *giggle snort* <i>&quot;a sensible garou, he says!&quot; </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T18:47:23-07:00","id":1562328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562296#post1562296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given they're only one person, it's literally impossible for this werewolf to really control a large area, assuming all they have going for themselves is being stronger.<br /> <br /> Their power only goes as far as their arms. To submit a Sept they have to leave the current one, to punish someone they have to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be underestimating exactly how well legacy WtA Garou can extend their reach. Moonbridges (and powers that use them to model their mechanics but don't rely on them specifically) allow the Garou to move insane distances in moments. There's a number of higher level powers (not just Gifts, also Rites which aren't Rank restricted) that do more to precisely let the upper eschelons of the Garou Nation control either gigantic areas of contiguous land, whole cities, or multiple smaller territories with vast distances between them.<br /> <br /> Their more positive relationship with spirits and some of the frankly absurd social Gifts also make building local forces to protect an area much easier for them than what W5 has on offer. So even if they have to leave, they can build up far better defenses to at least hold out until they return.<br /> <br /> As I said above, it doesn't make them invincible or unstoppable if enough W5 Garou unite against them, but that's also why I stressed how much their ability to push W20 mechanics into the hands of W5 characters would matter. If an Elder W20 Theurge and use the Gift that lets them complete rewrite a spirit... and that means reversing W5's status quo back to what spirits were like in W5's setting before everything went to shit, or even to just full blown W20 spirits... that's a lot of power with that alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-29T20:02:02-07:00","id":1562331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1557559-a-w20-wolf-in-w5?p=1562328#post1562328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might be underestimating exactly how well legacy WtA Garou can extend their reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand, but here's the thing: all those options work because they're support for an actual leader. They greatly increase the reach of a W20 Garou, but they don't make this reach work. And they require a particular build.<br /> <br /> The &quot;how hard they'll derail things from the sheer power imbalance they existence causes&quot; part precludes any complex plan. They count only with being generally too powerful, and in fact the very idea of taking control of anything is pushing beyond the original proposal. And the tangent about conquering Septs was for soloing them, which means we're not talking someone who'll count on additional forces to do the job.<br /> <br /> An actual Elder fitting for the setting with a clear plan can do a lot more. An actual scenario for the exercise is a completely different story. An actual structure for how the powers are working in W5 may go all the way from &quot;they won't really do much&quot; to &quot;this is how this particular character in this particular scenario would overhaul the whole thing and maybe even resurrect Gaia&quot;.<br /> <br /> But as a generic Garou going generic solo? No. Not even an Elder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-30T12:04:27-07:00","id":1562345,"title":"","content":"I've been saying from the beginning of all of this that of course it scales with the power of the individual in question, so I'm not sure what you're point is really. I was pointing out that you were understating the upper limits.<br /> <br /> It doesn't even require a specific build. Higher level Garou that weren't built to be leaders are going to develop some leadership skills to hold those Ranks and positions. They're going to learn how to enact plans. They're going to value the Garou Nation over the splintering of things that happened in W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}